WEBVTT

00:24.080 --> 00:26.780
You want to know who the strongest
man in the Kabuki District is?

00:27.100 --> 00:29.290
You must be new in town.

00:29.290 --> 00:32.580
You won't last long with that attitude.

00:32.580 --> 00:33.800
Forget it.

00:33.800 --> 00:35.290
This town is on a whole different level.

00:35.900 --> 00:38.980
You got thugs, brawlers,
vigilantes, and rogue warriors

00:38.980 --> 00:40.690
from all over Edo here.

00:40.690 --> 00:42.800
It's like a haven for hooligans.

00:43.070 --> 00:44.180
This is for your own good.

00:44.180 --> 00:46.970
Have a drink and go back
to the countryside.

00:49.060 --> 00:50.050
What's that?

00:50.050 --> 00:52.760
You want me to tell you about
the top dogs before you go?

00:52.760 --> 00:54.060
You really like this stuff.

00:54.600 --> 00:57.560
First, there are four monsters
on a level of their own.

00:58.050 --> 01:00.320
The Fierce and Divine
Mademoiselle Saigo.

01:00.320 --> 01:02.650
Jirocho Doromizu the Gallant.

01:02.650 --> 01:03.820
Peacock Princess Kada.

01:03.820 --> 01:05.070
Empress Otose.

01:05.360 --> 01:07.070
The four factions are in a

01:07.070 --> 01:09.650
standoff which preserves a
fragile balance of power.

01:10.560 --> 01:12.740
Who would be the strongest in a fight?

01:12.740 --> 01:15.450
You wouldn't be able to
even scratch those beasts.

01:15.990 --> 01:20.610
Saigo and Jirocho, in particular,
were heroes during the Joi War.

01:20.610 --> 01:23.840
Well, they're too old
to go on a tear now.

01:23.930 --> 01:25.840
If you want someone
who's currently active,

01:26.330 --> 01:28.120
there's Katsuo Kurogoma,

01:28.120 --> 01:29.970
a young leader in the Doromizu faction.

01:29.970 --> 01:33.220
He's the most feared man
in the Kabuki District now.

01:33.770 --> 01:37.050
You'll also find a few former
Joi in Saigo's faction.

01:37.050 --> 01:38.460
There are rumors about

01:38.460 --> 01:41.000
Kada's faction having
ties to some crazy folk.

01:44.170 --> 01:45.820
Otose's faction?

01:45.820 --> 01:48.150
Snack Otose

01:46.070 --> 01:48.150
It's just a bar, really.

01:48.320 --> 01:50.960
She's just an old lady
with a soft heart.

01:51.320 --> 01:56.030
But if you try any funny
business on her turf,

01:56.030 --> 01:58.580
you'll run into a certain guy.

01:59.060 --> 02:02.260
A guy who holds his own against
the Big Three by himself.

02:02.260 --> 02:04.090
One hell of a monster,

02:04.750 --> 02:06.460
with hair that's completely white.

02:13.170 --> 02:14.260
A demon...

02:17.840 --> 02:18.900
That's too bad.

02:19.370 --> 02:21.140
I was going to decorate your

02:21.140 --> 02:23.770
completely white head with
some bright red flowers.

02:24.280 --> 02:25.870
Your reputation precedes you.

02:26.150 --> 02:28.280
The strongest man in
the Kabuki District...

02:28.550 --> 02:29.900
Gintoki Sakata-san...

02:31.420 --> 02:33.690
Who are you...?

02:34.460 --> 02:37.340
I didn't realize how
strong you were, Bro!

02:37.550 --> 02:39.930
Could you take me in...

02:39.930 --> 02:42.220
...as one of your underlings?

02:42.920 --> 02:44.270
Odd Jobs Gin-chan

02:44.370 --> 02:45.670
It's freezing.

02:46.010 --> 02:48.030
It's always so cold in the morning.

02:50.900 --> 02:52.240
Who is she?

02:52.240 --> 02:53.120
A drunk?

02:53.380 --> 02:55.070
Uh, excuse me.

02:55.070 --> 02:57.120
You'll catch a cold if you sleep here.

02:57.580 --> 02:58.620
Excuse me.

02:58.620 --> 03:00.000
Your snot has frozen.

03:01.750 --> 03:03.380
Yikes, it's a raid!

03:04.350 --> 03:05.470
Wha-Wha-Wha--

03:05.470 --> 03:06.910
What are you doing?!

03:06.910 --> 03:08.800
Which gang are you from?

03:09.210 --> 03:11.470
If you try to lay a finger on my Bro,

03:11.470 --> 03:13.500
I'll make some bright red flowers.

03:13.500 --> 03:15.480
What are you babbling about?!

03:15.480 --> 03:16.540
Wait a moment here!

03:16.680 --> 03:18.230
Wait!

03:22.190 --> 03:23.860
It's too early for all this noise.

03:23.860 --> 03:25.360
Snack Otose

03:25.750 --> 03:30.240
I am the newest member of the
Odd Jobs gang, Pirako Chin.

03:30.240 --> 03:34.240
It is an honor to meet
the big boss Otose.

03:34.710 --> 03:36.440
I apologize for my behavior earlier.

03:36.440 --> 03:39.870
I didn't realize that you were
the Bro's number one underling.

03:40.200 --> 03:43.130
I'll make up for it by
cutting off my pinky.

03:44.290 --> 03:46.380
Hey, what the hell are you doing?

03:47.210 --> 03:48.790
I have nothing to do
with organized crime.

03:48.790 --> 03:50.520
And I don't want any underlings.

03:50.520 --> 03:52.060
And I told you to get lost already!

03:52.060 --> 03:53.090
You damn punk girl!

03:53.540 --> 03:54.790
You're tearing out my hair!

03:54.790 --> 03:57.170
The two of us can become the bosses

03:57.170 --> 03:59.210
of the underworld, Bro!

03:59.210 --> 04:01.350
When did I ever say that I
wanted to be Darth Vader!

04:01.730 --> 04:03.820
What's with her?

04:01.730 --> 04:05.210
Please! I have nowhere else to go!

04:05.220 --> 04:06.890
You come from a gang?

04:08.330 --> 04:09.780
I've heard rumors.

04:09.780 --> 04:11.810
The Uekibachi gang was having a

04:11.810 --> 04:13.700
business quarrel with Jirocho's people.

04:13.970 --> 04:17.380
When a fight broke out,
there was a crazy girl who

04:17.380 --> 04:19.850
took out the whole lot by herself.

04:20.110 --> 04:22.300
Her name was Pirako the killer.

04:23.510 --> 04:25.200
Huh?! A killer?!

04:25.200 --> 04:26.530
This little twit?!

04:26.530 --> 04:28.710
This little girl works
for the underworld?!

04:29.130 --> 04:31.620
It's nothing to brag about.

04:31.620 --> 04:34.220
I just happen to be good
at decorating with flowers.

04:34.670 --> 04:35.950
Did you know?

04:35.950 --> 04:37.290
The more evil someone is,

04:37.290 --> 04:38.980
the more beautiful a flower they make.

04:39.170 --> 04:42.730
And when I cut them up more, the
flowers are redder and prettier!

04:42.820 --> 04:44.560
Uh, I'm very sorry.

04:44.560 --> 04:46.260
I didn't mean to call you a little girl.

04:46.260 --> 04:47.320
You said you have nowhere to go?

04:47.320 --> 04:49.330
What happened to your former employers?

04:49.330 --> 04:50.740
They're dead.

04:50.920 --> 04:53.380
They were jumped by the Jirocho gang

04:53.380 --> 04:55.490
and turned into a lovely garden.

04:55.830 --> 04:57.830
There was a nice man
there who took me in,

04:57.830 --> 04:59.380
and I always did what I was told,

04:59.380 --> 05:01.590
so I don't know what to do now.

05:01.590 --> 05:05.000
But I only know how to
decorate with flowers.

05:05.340 --> 05:07.420
That's why I'm here.

05:07.420 --> 05:09.750
I'm here to turn the
town where Jirocho is...

05:09.750 --> 05:14.130
To turn the Kabuki District into a
garden of bright red flower garden!

05:15.890 --> 05:17.370
Hey, hey, hey!

05:17.370 --> 05:18.760
The Bro is passin' through!

05:19.150 --> 05:22.270
Whatcha lookin' at, twerps? Eh?!

05:22.420 --> 05:24.310
You wanna make something of it?!

05:24.310 --> 05:26.020
Wanna make something of it?!

05:26.270 --> 05:27.820
This is bad. Very bad.

05:27.820 --> 05:29.520
We've picked up a really dangerous girl.

05:29.770 --> 05:31.750
She said she's going to turn the
Kabuki District into a flower garden.

05:31.750 --> 05:33.550
She means a sea of blood, doesn't she?

05:33.550 --> 05:37.280
She wants to use your strength
to get revenge on Jirocho.

05:37.690 --> 05:39.350
I-It'll be okay.

05:39.350 --> 05:41.290
Hey! Wanna fight?

05:39.350 --> 05:41.790
She's a killer, but she's just a girl.

05:41.940 --> 05:44.640
She can't be stupid enough
to take on the big boss...

05:44.640 --> 05:46.560
Look here, Bro!

05:46.700 --> 05:48.100
Pretty flowers!

05:48.100 --> 05:48.830
See?

05:48.830 --> 05:50.630
She looks like a perfectly normal girl

05:50.630 --> 05:51.800
who happens to like flowers...

05:52.180 --> 05:54.540
Gran, you been payin' all your fees?

05:54.540 --> 05:55.300
Eh?!

05:55.740 --> 05:58.630
Don't make threats with
a smile on your face!

05:58.630 --> 06:01.960
A gang needs money to run.

06:01.960 --> 06:04.270
In return, we provide security.

06:04.570 --> 06:07.230
They're looking for security from us!

06:07.600 --> 06:08.570
Now listen to me.

06:08.570 --> 06:10.460
If you want to join Odd Jobs,

06:10.460 --> 06:12.480
forget all that dark side stuff.

06:12.480 --> 06:14.360
You aren't Darth Vader.

06:14.360 --> 06:15.990
You're just an ordinary girl.

06:16.320 --> 06:18.430
You aren't Pirako Chin.

06:18.430 --> 06:20.080
From now on, you're Birako Man.

06:20.080 --> 06:21.240
What kind of name is that?!

06:21.680 --> 06:22.560
Understood.

06:22.560 --> 06:23.850
I'm Birabirako Man.

06:23.850 --> 06:24.970
No, you have an extra "bira" in there!

06:24.970 --> 06:25.920
Could you stop that?!

06:25.920 --> 06:28.560
Hey, there's a cute
cake place over there!

06:28.560 --> 06:32.900
You can learn how to be a girl
there, Birabirabirabirako Man!

06:32.900 --> 06:34.510
Enough with the "birabira" already!

06:34.780 --> 06:36.760
This is kind of embarrassing.

06:36.980 --> 06:39.180
I've never been in a
place like this before.

06:39.180 --> 06:40.510
Do I stand out?

06:40.710 --> 06:42.110
Not at all.

06:42.110 --> 06:43.940
You look perfectly natural here!

06:43.940 --> 06:46.020
You guys stand out like sore thumbs.

06:46.580 --> 06:49.110
Don't worry about it,
Birabirabirabirako-san.

06:49.360 --> 06:51.250
You look like a very normal...

06:51.250 --> 06:53.270
No, a very cute girl.

06:53.270 --> 06:53.780
Huh?

06:54.280 --> 06:56.030
You should drop the gangster act.

06:56.030 --> 06:56.840
It's such a waste.

06:56.840 --> 06:59.280
Oh, sorry about trying
to boss you around.

06:59.980 --> 07:01.960
Come on, what are you doing?

07:01.960 --> 07:03.030
Eat your cake.

07:03.530 --> 07:05.920
If you don't eat your cake, I'll eat it.

07:09.390 --> 07:11.680
A cockroach was chewing on my cake.

07:11.680 --> 07:13.930
It's too dirty for me to eat.

07:13.930 --> 07:16.130
What are you going to
do about this, dammit?

07:16.510 --> 07:18.580
Hey! Are you saying I'm a cockroach?!

07:18.580 --> 07:20.700
I'm actually kind of a clean freak.

07:20.700 --> 07:22.470
Gangster stuff aside.

07:22.470 --> 07:23.760
Gangster stuff aside?!

07:22.470 --> 07:33.480
Morimioto Candy

07:23.760 --> 07:25.920
So you just hate me, period?!

07:25.920 --> 07:27.300
No sweat. That wasn't your fault.

07:27.300 --> 07:28.010
Nothing wrong there.

07:28.010 --> 07:29.550
That's how a normal girl would react.

07:29.550 --> 07:30.900
Why are you defending her?!

07:30.900 --> 07:33.480
Don't make it sound like every
single girl is anti-Shinpachi!

07:33.840 --> 07:37.360
If you act gangster again,
you get another "bira" tacked on.

07:37.360 --> 07:39.470
At least your name will feel more girly,

07:39.470 --> 07:41.320
Birabirabirabirabirako Man.

07:41.320 --> 07:42.790
How is that name girly?!

07:42.790 --> 07:44.710
It makes her sound like
a "birabira" monster!

07:44.710 --> 07:46.080
Enough already!

07:46.080 --> 07:49.410
Hey, there's a cute
dried fish place, *****!

07:49.410 --> 07:50.500
Watch your mouth!

07:50.730 --> 07:52.500
Whoa, look at this, Birako Man!

07:52.500 --> 07:54.790
They're all dried! They're all hard!

07:54.790 --> 07:56.410
And wait, you're just taking

07:54.790 --> 07:56.920
Ooh, it's so cute!

07:56.410 --> 07:58.130
her to the places you want to go!

07:56.920 --> 07:59.090
Why is it so dry?

07:58.130 --> 08:00.510
What's so girly about dried fish?!

08:00.920 --> 08:02.220
Bro!

08:02.750 --> 08:03.720
Oh, sorry...

08:05.700 --> 08:08.220
Bro! What's wrong?!

08:07.240 --> 08:08.240
It's broken!

08:08.240 --> 08:10.520
The impact broke it!

08:10.970 --> 08:12.900
Here comes the real thing!

08:12.900 --> 08:13.980
This is bad.

08:12.900 --> 08:13.980
Hey, girl!

08:13.980 --> 08:15.040
We were making progress,

08:13.980 --> 08:17.230
Whatcha gonna do about this?

08:15.040 --> 08:17.220
but they're going to stimulate
her gangster blood.

08:16.490 --> 08:17.780
Gran, give me some sukonbu.

08:18.230 --> 08:20.730
If they're from Jirocho's faction...

08:20.730 --> 08:22.820
Bah, can't help it.

08:23.030 --> 08:25.120
Gin-san! No violence!

08:25.140 --> 08:26.330
I know.

08:26.330 --> 08:28.790
I'll settle this in a mature
and gentlemanly fashion.

08:30.400 --> 08:33.170
Excuse me, did my friend
do something wrong?

08:33.170 --> 08:34.920
Huh? Who are you?

08:36.150 --> 08:37.120
B-Bro!

08:37.120 --> 08:38.320
What's wrong?

08:38.320 --> 08:39.930
I-It's broken...

08:39.930 --> 08:43.720
Th-The pat on the shoulder
shattered all of my bones!

08:44.050 --> 08:46.260
You're doing the exact same thing!

08:46.420 --> 08:48.510
What do you mean, pat on the shoulder?

08:48.510 --> 08:50.410
You're the one who patted
me on the shoulder!

08:50.410 --> 08:53.240
So, what are you going to do about this?

08:53.240 --> 08:54.060
Hey!

08:54.060 --> 08:55.610
You're making it worse!

08:55.860 --> 08:57.860
That won't do! Calm down, Birako!

08:57.870 --> 08:59.440
Here's your change.

09:00.440 --> 09:02.130
Why are you pretending
to break your bones?!

09:02.420 --> 09:04.140
Uh, you broke your arm,

09:04.140 --> 09:06.460
while two of us broke all of our bones.

09:06.460 --> 09:08.130
Can we call it even?

09:08.130 --> 09:10.620
You broke your own bones!

09:10.620 --> 09:13.360
That girl wasn't anywhere near us!

09:13.820 --> 09:15.470
Bro, that's enough.

09:15.470 --> 09:17.870
He's the one who's with Otose...

09:17.870 --> 09:18.530
What?

09:19.080 --> 09:20.250
Oh...

09:20.250 --> 09:23.250
He's the one who took
on Big Bro Katsuo...

09:23.250 --> 09:24.660
Katsuo Kurogoma...

09:24.660 --> 09:26.250
So they belong to Jirocho's gang.

09:26.390 --> 09:29.580
All of my bones have been broken...

09:29.580 --> 09:31.190
Could you let this one slide?

09:31.190 --> 09:32.590
B-Bro, we should go...

09:32.590 --> 09:34.970
I'll let you go today.

09:35.660 --> 09:36.770
Now come with me.

09:36.770 --> 09:37.450
Huh?

09:37.560 --> 09:39.200
I don't have any business with him,

09:39.200 --> 09:42.080
but I'll need you to pay up

09:42.080 --> 09:43.960
by using that body of yours...

09:44.460 --> 09:46.500
N-No! Bro!

09:46.520 --> 09:47.630
Please wait a moment!

09:47.630 --> 09:49.210
Stop struggling!

09:49.550 --> 09:51.420
You damn bitch!

09:52.990 --> 09:54.040
Huh?

09:54.040 --> 09:56.260
I thought your bones were all broken?

09:56.560 --> 09:57.440
And your arm?

09:57.700 --> 10:00.270
It seems to be in...

10:00.560 --> 10:02.770
...terrible shape!

10:05.260 --> 10:06.090
Bro!

10:06.580 --> 10:08.300
Snap out of it, Bro!

10:08.260 --> 10:10.190
Matsuo to Kiyoshi

10:08.600 --> 10:10.060
Wha-Wha--

10:08.800 --> 10:10.060
Bro!

10:10.060 --> 10:12.720
Wake up, Bro!

10:10.250 --> 10:12.230
What the hell are you doing?!

10:12.230 --> 10:14.590
Why did you make the first move?!

10:14.590 --> 10:18.260
Well, he was taking advantage
of my gracious behavior.

10:18.260 --> 10:19.660
I just gave him a little flick.

10:19.660 --> 10:20.420
The hell you did!

10:20.420 --> 10:21.820
You sent him flying through the air!

10:21.820 --> 10:23.310
You rule, Bro!

10:23.310 --> 10:24.760
I think I'm in love.

10:24.760 --> 10:28.580
Now we have no choice but to
fight it out with Jirocho.

10:28.580 --> 10:30.900
Together, we can make
lots of red flowers

10:30.900 --> 10:33.660
and become the bosses of Japan.

10:34.390 --> 10:35.740
Damn it!

10:35.740 --> 10:37.290
You tricked me!

10:37.720 --> 10:38.510
Bastards!

10:37.720 --> 10:39.290
That's not funny!

10:38.510 --> 10:40.790
You won't get away with this!

10:39.290 --> 10:41.300
I'm not gonna pick a fight with Jirocho!

10:40.790 --> 10:41.980
This means war!

10:41.980 --> 10:43.490
I ain't gonna fight a war!

10:43.510 --> 10:46.050
Gin-san! You're starting
the war as we speak!

10:46.430 --> 10:47.490
Pipe down!

10:47.490 --> 10:48.490
Calm yourself!

10:48.490 --> 10:50.690
Calm yourself and look
around for Dryaemon.

10:50.690 --> 10:51.560
You need to calm down!

10:51.760 --> 10:53.940
It's okay, Ginta-kun!

10:53.940 --> 10:55.060
I have just what you need!

10:55.060 --> 10:57.240
Ready-mix concrete!

10:57.240 --> 10:58.850
What are you going to do with that?!

10:58.850 --> 10:59.240
Shut up!

10:58.850 --> 11:10.490
Matsuo to Kiyoshi

10:59.240 --> 11:01.080
If we stick Giannosuke
and Suneorochimaru

11:01.080 --> 11:02.900
in here and toss it in the ocean,

11:02.900 --> 11:05.830
we can basically shut them up forever!

11:05.830 --> 11:07.960
Lady Shizuka will be yours!

11:07.960 --> 11:08.820
Hell no!

11:09.060 --> 11:10.130
You'll scare off Lady Shizuka!

11:10.460 --> 11:13.870
Pops, give me the usual dog food...

11:14.610 --> 11:17.130
Looks like a fight's going down.

11:17.480 --> 11:18.510
What's...

11:21.010 --> 11:25.640
Kabuki District Council
Meeting Room

11:21.260 --> 11:25.640
We will now begin the Ka-Kabuki
District Council Meeting.

11:25.640 --> 11:31.650
Kabuki District
Clean Up Project

11:26.160 --> 11:29.600
The topic today is separating trash...

11:31.910 --> 11:33.400
Get lost, trash.

11:33.400 --> 11:34.380
Yes!

11:34.380 --> 11:35.780
Excuse me!

11:41.520 --> 11:43.110
So what's this about?

11:42.700 --> 11:47.290
The Kabuki District's Empress Otose

11:43.110 --> 11:44.930
Why did you call us here?

11:44.930 --> 11:47.290
I don't recall ever failing
to separate my trash.

11:47.290 --> 11:48.910
You just did.

11:48.910 --> 11:51.590
Why is this stinkin' garbage of a hag

11:49.080 --> 11:56.130
The Fierce and Divine Mademoiselle Saigo

11:51.590 --> 11:54.110
mixed in with us beauties?

11:54.110 --> 11:56.130
You shouldn't be talking.

11:56.920 --> 12:02.140
Peacock Princess Kada

11:57.160 --> 11:59.780
I'm glad to see that
you haven't changed.

11:59.760 --> 12:02.140
I apologize for taking up your time.

12:02.640 --> 12:04.020
But you'll have to wait a little longer.

12:04.020 --> 12:05.850
We're missing a member.

12:05.850 --> 12:07.140
Jirocho?

12:07.140 --> 12:08.200
There's no point.

12:08.200 --> 12:11.350
It's been two or three years
since he was last seen in public.

12:11.860 --> 12:16.060
I was hoping to have all four
Devas present for this discussion.

12:16.360 --> 12:19.610
I called you here for one reason.

12:20.180 --> 12:22.310
You are probably aware that

12:22.310 --> 12:25.620
the town has grown tense
the past few years.

12:26.410 --> 12:29.270
If nothing is done,
a war will break out.

12:29.270 --> 12:32.670
I'm sure that nobody wishes
for that to happen.

12:32.670 --> 12:34.300
Listen to yourself.

12:34.300 --> 12:37.960
You and Jirocho are the
ones making a splash.

12:38.290 --> 12:39.810
It used to be that the casinos

12:39.810 --> 12:42.080
in this town were run by Jirocho's gang.

12:42.080 --> 12:45.300
But then you built a casino here.

12:45.580 --> 12:48.400
The same could be said of you, Saigo.

12:48.720 --> 12:50.430
I've heard tales

12:50.940 --> 12:54.110
that you're sheltering Joi
patriots and rogue warriors.

12:54.110 --> 12:54.690
Huh?

12:55.170 --> 12:57.340
Your soldiers may be dressed oddly,

12:57.340 --> 13:00.250
but each one of them is quite strong.

13:00.250 --> 13:01.780
You plan on using their strength

13:01.780 --> 13:04.200
to create an empire of trannies...

13:04.200 --> 13:06.180
What are you talking about?

13:06.180 --> 13:08.700
I'm offering a home to those
who have no place to go.

13:08.700 --> 13:12.290
But the fact remains that
you've repeatedly refused

13:12.290 --> 13:15.710
to accept the demands of Jirocho's gang.

13:16.340 --> 13:17.830
And Otose...

13:17.830 --> 13:20.440
I have no interest in your stupid fight,

13:20.440 --> 13:22.300
and I'll have none of it.

13:22.510 --> 13:23.620
You may have no interest,

13:23.620 --> 13:26.800
but you've always held great
influence in this town.

13:26.800 --> 13:28.890
I've heard that you listen to the

13:28.890 --> 13:31.810
problems of your customers
and offer counseling.

13:32.340 --> 13:35.690
And your pawns in that
sketchy Odd Jobs group

13:35.690 --> 13:38.030
provide the necessary assistance.

13:38.030 --> 13:41.320
They've been running wild
across our territory.

13:41.910 --> 13:46.450
I never knew that I had
pawns I could order around.

13:46.450 --> 13:49.370
And I never knew that this town

13:49.370 --> 13:51.840
had been divided up into territories.

13:53.920 --> 13:56.410
This town doesn't belong to anyone.

13:56.900 --> 14:00.840
We just live our lives here.

14:01.270 --> 14:02.980
That's all.

14:03.520 --> 14:06.260
However, some are not satisfied by that.

14:06.900 --> 14:10.080
These days, we are
known as the Four Devas

14:10.080 --> 14:13.020
who work together to run this town,

14:13.390 --> 14:17.030
but didn't it all begin with the

14:17.030 --> 14:20.400
rise of a new faction,
a king of hooligans?

14:20.860 --> 14:23.670
There is no reason for us to fight.

14:23.670 --> 14:25.590
After all,

14:26.070 --> 14:28.160
isn't our enemy Jirocho?

14:28.160 --> 14:30.160
I see how it is.

14:30.360 --> 14:32.590
The three of you are teaming up

14:32.590 --> 14:35.160
to get rid of Jirocho, the obstacle.

14:35.990 --> 14:37.000
Well, well.

14:37.350 --> 14:39.000
Wait up!

14:39.000 --> 14:41.380
It's over! This is war!

14:41.380 --> 14:42.930
This is all-out war!

14:42.930 --> 14:43.630
Gin-san!

14:43.630 --> 14:45.490
This is out of control!

14:45.490 --> 14:48.510
Ginta-kun is off on a
rendezvous with Lady Shizuka.

14:48.510 --> 14:49.430
Huh?!

14:49.430 --> 14:52.050
The bastard used us as decoys!

14:52.050 --> 14:54.740
I'll get you for this!

15:01.200 --> 15:03.690
It looks like they're gone, Bro.

15:04.700 --> 15:06.950
Things are getting fun.

15:07.160 --> 15:09.290
What's so fun about this?

15:09.290 --> 15:11.690
Time to bust out an old cliche.

15:12.200 --> 15:15.960
Revenge isn't fun for anyone.

15:16.470 --> 15:18.090
I'm sure that your dead friends

15:18.090 --> 15:20.470
would want you to live
like an ordinary girl

15:20.570 --> 15:23.890
instead of letting revenge
take over your life.

15:25.110 --> 15:26.160
Bro...

15:26.800 --> 15:30.710
Why do you keep talking about revenge?

15:30.710 --> 15:34.710
Uh, wasn't your gang
slaughtered by Jirocho?

15:34.710 --> 15:36.420
So you want revenge...

15:36.440 --> 15:38.220
What are you talking about?

15:38.220 --> 15:41.080
My gang was crushed by Jirocho,

15:41.080 --> 15:42.420
but they're all alive.

15:42.480 --> 15:43.250
Huh?

15:43.250 --> 15:44.710
But you said they were
turned into a flower garden.

15:45.070 --> 15:48.260
They quit the business
to become farmers.

15:48.260 --> 15:49.210
They've planted a garden of red flowers.

15:49.520 --> 15:51.370
It's a pretty place.

15:51.370 --> 15:55.220
But it was boring, so I left.

15:55.590 --> 15:56.440
Huh?!

15:56.440 --> 15:58.850
Could you be any more misleading?!

15:59.020 --> 16:02.180
We've been trying to subtly convince you

16:02.180 --> 16:06.590
to give up on revenge because
of your dark past...

16:06.590 --> 16:07.650
So wait?

16:07.650 --> 16:09.980
Why are you here?

16:10.900 --> 16:12.070
Like I said,

16:12.080 --> 16:15.860
I'm here to decorate Jirocho
and this town in red flowers.

16:15.860 --> 16:16.710
Enough of that.

16:16.710 --> 16:17.990
Give it to me straight.

16:17.990 --> 16:19.740
I mean exactly what I say.

16:20.160 --> 16:24.750
I'm here to help the great
Jirocho bloom again.

16:24.950 --> 16:26.060
For that,

16:26.060 --> 16:28.900
I need the help of the strongest
man in the Kabuki District!

16:28.900 --> 16:30.660
That's you, Bro!

16:30.690 --> 16:31.810
Got it.

16:31.810 --> 16:35.390
In other words, your
mind is full of flowers,

16:35.390 --> 16:37.630
and it's a waste of time
to bother talking with you.

16:38.180 --> 16:40.720
In that case, this is farewell...

16:47.120 --> 16:52.900
Bro, the bond between gang
members isn't easily broken.

16:52.900 --> 16:55.590
I don't have a bond with
a plastic trash can!

16:55.900 --> 16:57.680
The concrete's hard now!

16:57.680 --> 17:00.590
This is all because you kept on talking!

17:00.590 --> 17:01.610
What do we do?!

17:01.610 --> 17:03.100
What's going to happen?!

17:03.100 --> 17:05.100
Well, that's easy enough.

17:05.100 --> 17:07.850
You get served the treatment

17:08.090 --> 17:10.230
you were gonna deal.

17:12.790 --> 17:14.610
Y-You're...

17:15.080 --> 17:17.280
Sorry to keep you waiting.

17:17.760 --> 17:19.780
The obstacle's here.

17:20.530 --> 17:22.530
Jirocho...

17:22.530 --> 17:24.200
Don't mind me.

17:24.200 --> 17:26.030
Carry on.

17:26.440 --> 17:30.410
I believe the three of you were talking
about teaming up to get rid of me?

17:30.660 --> 17:33.530
We never said anything about that.

17:33.530 --> 17:36.420
I simply mentioned that our wish
to avoid any pointless conflict

17:36.420 --> 17:40.420
was being ruined by an
unstoppable loose cannon.

17:40.640 --> 17:42.900
I would take him out.

17:42.900 --> 17:46.930
Some fools in this world
can only be cured by death.

17:47.220 --> 17:50.680
But I wouldn't arrange
a meeting like this.

17:50.680 --> 17:51.810
Look.

17:51.810 --> 17:56.310
Your necks are all lined up
within range of my blade.

17:59.320 --> 18:01.540
One of the Peacock Princess's pets, huh?

18:01.540 --> 18:02.360
Stand down.

18:02.360 --> 18:03.490
He's merely joking.

18:03.760 --> 18:06.960
No, he made the correct decision.

18:06.960 --> 18:11.830
This pet was trained well to
be able to detect my hostility.

18:12.520 --> 18:15.580
Unfortunately, I'm getting old,

18:15.580 --> 18:18.850
so I have trouble controlling
my piss and my hostility.

18:18.850 --> 18:22.090
I already sheathed my blade,
but it keeps trickling out...

18:22.570 --> 18:24.410
Case in point.

18:24.410 --> 18:28.620
You didn't notice me taking you out.

18:31.430 --> 18:33.690
I said to stop this!

18:33.980 --> 18:35.770
What do you think you're
doing to the boss?!

18:35.770 --> 18:36.580
Take them!

18:36.580 --> 18:38.290
You've shown your true colors!

18:38.290 --> 18:40.150
We won't let you lay a finger on Mama!

18:46.170 --> 18:49.080
You were eavesdropping on a
conversation between ladies?

18:49.510 --> 18:53.460
You bastards ready to have
your balls ripped out?!

18:53.620 --> 18:55.290
Stand down, boys.

18:55.290 --> 18:56.190
Boss!

19:00.320 --> 19:02.710
Ordinary humans have no place here.

19:05.120 --> 19:06.220
Good grief.

19:06.490 --> 19:10.060
How do you intend to
stop these monsters?

19:10.060 --> 19:13.230
If you have any ideas,
I'd love to hear them.

19:13.230 --> 19:18.760
As you saw, power can only
be restrained by more power.

19:19.100 --> 19:20.730
Here is my proposal.

19:21.260 --> 19:23.930
The factions of the Four Devas are

19:23.930 --> 19:26.660
not allowed to engage
in personal fights.

19:26.940 --> 19:32.190
The faction which breaks this rule

19:32.190 --> 19:35.140
will be crushed by the other three.

19:36.840 --> 19:39.210
So in the end, it'll still be the three

19:39.210 --> 19:41.880
of you teaming up against me?

19:42.830 --> 19:47.930
You think you can take
my balls by teaming up?

19:48.180 --> 19:49.810
Don't get the wrong idea.

19:49.810 --> 19:52.430
This rule is to prevent
further conflict.

19:52.670 --> 19:56.940
The town will be a dull
place if nobody can fight.

19:57.210 --> 20:01.690
If that's the only way to
avoid a war, then so be it.

20:02.830 --> 20:05.070
Are you sane?

20:05.070 --> 20:06.870
Very well.

20:06.870 --> 20:08.970
It'll be a test of endurance.

20:09.000 --> 20:15.190
Try not to screw up before I do.

20:15.900 --> 20:16.950
Boss!

20:16.950 --> 20:18.660
You really sure about this?

20:19.020 --> 20:20.650
If one faction causes trouble,

20:20.650 --> 20:23.320
the other three gang up to crush it?

20:23.400 --> 20:26.670
It's obvious that they
want to get rid of us!

20:27.080 --> 20:29.830
I'd say that this saves time.

20:29.830 --> 20:32.120
This is a chance to show them who the

20:32.120 --> 20:34.010
real king of the Kabuki District is.

20:34.220 --> 20:37.640
But that means we'll have
to deal with Otose...

20:38.060 --> 20:40.920
My memory's been getting worse.

20:41.300 --> 20:43.640
Who is this Otose person?

20:44.520 --> 20:45.530
Idiot!

20:45.530 --> 20:47.120
We're not supposed to mention the hag

20:47.120 --> 20:48.450
while the boss is around!

20:48.540 --> 20:53.310
The vixen is not as much
of a concern as the cub.

20:53.310 --> 20:55.410
Focus on him.

20:55.730 --> 20:56.720
Damn.

20:56.720 --> 20:59.410
What is that kid doing?

21:02.360 --> 21:04.120
You were dancing to her tune.

21:04.460 --> 21:05.790
That's not like you.

21:06.250 --> 21:08.960
Kada is using you to get rid of Jirocho,

21:08.960 --> 21:11.800
who's hurting her business.

21:12.160 --> 21:13.950
I just want to live peacefully

21:13.950 --> 21:16.160
in this town with my comrades.

21:16.310 --> 21:19.890
I'll dance a waltz or octopus
dance if that's what it takes.

21:20.400 --> 21:23.830
So you can clean up this
town by eliminating him?

21:24.190 --> 21:25.640
Even if that were true,

21:26.100 --> 21:28.350
I could never bring
myself to love a town

21:28.350 --> 21:29.900
that's neat and tidy.

21:29.900 --> 21:32.170
Spoken like a true trashy old hag.

21:32.170 --> 21:33.260
I believe that you're old friends

21:33.260 --> 21:34.530
with the trashy old geezer?

21:35.070 --> 21:36.980
Haven't talked to him in over ten years.

21:37.340 --> 21:41.100
Doesn't really matter if a
dangerous old man dies or not.

21:41.370 --> 21:42.040
But...

21:42.710 --> 21:44.420
<i>I'm here to turn the town </i>

21:44.420 --> 21:46.190
<i>where Jirocho is into a garden.</i>

21:47.040 --> 21:49.790
The timing's too perfect.

21:50.360 --> 21:53.110
Finally, it's time for payback.

21:53.410 --> 21:55.090
Like I said before,

21:55.090 --> 21:59.050
I always return the
favor, seven for three.

21:59.430 --> 22:01.650
Nobody parts their hair 7:3 anymore.

22:01.650 --> 22:03.230
You should shave your head

22:03.230 --> 22:05.160
and opt for the bald look.

22:05.160 --> 22:06.200
Up yours!

22:06.200 --> 22:09.720
My hair is styled like Joe Odagiri!

22:09.720 --> 22:11.820
Fashion trends come back in a cycle!

22:12.060 --> 22:12.800
Hold on here.

22:12.800 --> 22:15.090
I was egged on by this stupid girl.

22:15.090 --> 22:17.520
I have no grudge against you, Joe Schmo.

22:17.520 --> 22:19.200
Who are you calling Joe Schmo?!

22:19.450 --> 22:22.450
Besides, that's not what
my boy here told me.

22:22.830 --> 22:23.960
I know what's going down.

22:23.960 --> 22:25.000
You promised to

22:25.000 --> 22:27.130
help her decorate our
boss with red flowers.

22:27.660 --> 22:28.460
How do you know that?

22:28.830 --> 22:31.330
Why don't you tell him what you really

22:31.330 --> 22:33.710
mean when you say red
flowers, Pirako-han?

22:34.060 --> 22:35.530
Uh, Pirako-chan?

22:35.750 --> 22:38.280
U-Uh, are you...

22:38.750 --> 22:41.270
Bro, my boss was

22:41.270 --> 22:45.220
a relative of Jirocho,
and an old friend.

22:46.050 --> 22:48.780
He used to tell me when I was young,

22:48.780 --> 22:53.480
about the great Jirocho,
warrior among warriors.

22:54.630 --> 22:56.580
The warriors you see around these days

22:56.580 --> 22:58.290
are just a bunch of wild hotheads.

22:58.290 --> 23:00.490
But he was different.

23:01.130 --> 23:03.630
He would save the weak
and crush the strong.

23:03.810 --> 23:05.230
He would only employ his strength

23:05.230 --> 23:07.120
for the sake of his particular justice.

23:07.670 --> 23:10.250
That's what you call a true warrior.

23:10.430 --> 23:13.090
That's too hard for me to understand.

23:13.700 --> 23:15.060
Sorry about that.

23:15.260 --> 23:18.390
The more I talk, the less sense I make.

23:18.660 --> 23:22.640
Basically, Jirocho was a flowery man.

23:23.190 --> 23:28.040
That's probably what
drew your mother to him.

23:28.250 --> 23:32.250
Though the flowers in him
died at some point...

23:34.140 --> 23:36.000
He abandoned his wife and child,

23:36.000 --> 23:38.890
and crushed his wife's
family because of business.

23:39.510 --> 23:41.660
And now he's picking a stupid fight

23:41.660 --> 23:44.890
with a tranny and an old hag.

23:47.160 --> 23:51.440
I just want to see the old
Jirocho one more time.

23:52.010 --> 23:54.380
To help him take the world...

23:54.380 --> 23:59.180
To help make some pretty
flowers bloom in my old man.

24:00.330 --> 24:02.310
Huh? What's she talking about?

24:02.310 --> 24:03.730
That went completely over my head.

24:04.080 --> 24:05.710
What? What?!

24:05.990 --> 24:07.410
There you have it.

24:07.410 --> 24:08.410
Pirako-han is...

24:08.410 --> 24:09.950
No, the young lady is

24:11.150 --> 24:12.720
Jirocho's daughter!

24:13.080 --> 24:15.100
To be precise, she's the daughter of the

24:15.100 --> 24:17.080
missus who divorced the boss
and went back to her family.

24:17.080 --> 24:18.280
Bullshit!

24:18.280 --> 24:19.710
Help your old man take the world?!

24:19.710 --> 24:22.360
That's the complete opposite of revenge!

24:22.680 --> 24:24.890
Isn't that what I said?

24:24.890 --> 24:26.580
I'm here to decorate him with flowers.

24:26.580 --> 24:29.720
You were talking about making
me the big boss of Japan!

24:29.720 --> 24:32.040
You were trying to
make me fight Jirocho!

24:32.040 --> 24:36.970
Yakuza grow stronger by recruiting
the people they beat.

24:36.970 --> 24:39.320
My old man can take the
world if the strongest

24:39.320 --> 24:41.270
man in the Kabuki
district is on his side.

24:41.370 --> 24:42.950
Once you're the big boss,

24:42.950 --> 24:44.880
my old man will be the big, big boss!

24:45.180 --> 24:47.660
Young lady, it's settled.

24:48.510 --> 24:52.060
Bro, the Jirocho gang will
be making their move now.

24:52.290 --> 24:54.140
Do you know what's happened?

24:54.440 --> 24:57.220
There's a law in this lawless town now.

24:57.390 --> 24:59.700
If any faction starts a fight,

24:59.700 --> 25:02.440
the other Devas will crush them.

25:02.730 --> 25:04.900
The first victim will probably be

25:04.900 --> 25:06.700
the boss of a certain someone

25:06.700 --> 25:08.460
who picked a fight with the Jirocho gang

25:08.460 --> 25:10.430
over a helpless little girl, Otose.

25:11.400 --> 25:13.560
But it's your call to make, Bro.

25:13.830 --> 25:16.030
Please join us!

25:16.230 --> 25:19.030
Or else we'll have to
drop you in the ocean,

25:19.030 --> 25:22.540
and Otose will be targeted by
everyone in the Kabuki district!

25:22.770 --> 25:25.760
Hey, I'm guessing that's
supposed to be a threat,

25:25.760 --> 25:27.320
but if you kill me here,

25:27.320 --> 25:29.880
you'll be considered the aggressors.

25:30.500 --> 25:32.020
You an idiot?

25:32.020 --> 25:33.950
Why do you think we put on a show

25:33.950 --> 25:35.770
in the middle of town?!

25:35.770 --> 25:37.510
We got plenty of witnesses!

25:37.810 --> 25:39.200
You're the idiots!

25:39.200 --> 25:41.950
The Four Devas aren't gonna
move because of a little spat!

25:41.950 --> 25:44.640
A death is far more serious!

25:44.640 --> 25:45.370
Die, baldie!

25:45.370 --> 25:46.620
Go bald down your parted hair line!

25:46.620 --> 25:47.480
Go bald all over your body!

25:47.480 --> 25:48.320
I ain't gonna go bald!

25:48.320 --> 25:50.550
Every week, I part my
hair to the opposite side

25:50.550 --> 25:53.030
to avoid excessive damage to my scalp!

25:53.030 --> 25:55.570
I ain't like Sanshi Katsura!

25:57.510 --> 26:00.780
If that's not enough, how's this?

26:00.970 --> 26:03.020
We'll say that you killed
our young leader here,

26:03.020 --> 26:04.880
and we killed you for revenge.

26:04.880 --> 26:07.280
Huh? No way...

26:12.720 --> 26:13.970
Bro!

26:14.200 --> 26:17.180
Is your boss the guy
with the parted hair?

26:17.180 --> 26:18.690
Or is it Jirocho?

26:18.690 --> 26:19.670
B-But...

26:19.670 --> 26:22.730
If you move, I'll turn
you all into flowers.

26:25.660 --> 26:27.850
Got it, Bro?

26:28.310 --> 26:30.230
I'm serious.

26:30.470 --> 26:33.240
D-Damn you!

26:35.860 --> 26:36.850
Bastard!

26:36.850 --> 26:38.580
He jumped into the water
with the concrete!

26:38.580 --> 26:40.080
Is he trying to escape?!

26:40.080 --> 26:41.250
Nope.

26:41.250 --> 26:42.800
He went to save him.

26:43.370 --> 26:44.460
That's stupid!

26:44.460 --> 26:45.500
He can't move!

26:45.500 --> 26:46.620
And why would he save Bro?!

26:47.120 --> 26:49.590
Yes, he's stupid.

26:49.590 --> 26:51.830
I was very surprised.

26:51.890 --> 26:55.880
But that's why I wanted him on our side.

26:56.370 --> 26:59.350
But he also chose the old hag.

27:00.100 --> 27:01.190
Pity.

27:01.700 --> 27:03.630
Bye-bye, Bro.

27:04.950 --> 27:06.390
Pity.

27:06.730 --> 27:10.460
I came up with this
plan so the three of us

27:10.460 --> 27:12.150
could deal with Jirocho,

27:12.530 --> 27:14.990
but I never would have
expected Otose to...

27:15.230 --> 27:16.780
Don't be ridiculous!

27:16.960 --> 27:18.320
Otose-san would never...

27:18.320 --> 27:20.530
Pako would never do anything like that!

27:20.530 --> 27:24.150
We know how gentle they are!

27:24.150 --> 27:25.660
Calm down, Assmi!

27:25.660 --> 27:26.580
Don't call me Assmi!

27:26.580 --> 27:27.740
It's Azumi, damn it!

27:27.740 --> 27:30.170
Shut the hell up, Ass!

27:31.310 --> 27:33.100
Could you add the "mi"?

27:33.100 --> 27:35.640
You can call me Assmi as
long as the "mi" is there.

27:37.950 --> 27:40.680
It looks like we were the only ones

27:40.680 --> 27:43.680
serious about stopping this conflict.

27:44.540 --> 27:47.440
When did you make a deal with Jirocho?

27:47.590 --> 27:50.440
You think I would make
a deal with that vixen?

27:52.420 --> 27:54.950
Were you pushed by the kid?

27:54.950 --> 27:58.200
No, were you the one who pushed the kid?

27:58.470 --> 28:00.420
Don't play dumb!

28:00.420 --> 28:03.930
They might be rotten to the core,

28:03.930 --> 28:06.040
but they aren't dirty like you people!

28:06.040 --> 28:07.680
That's enough.

28:07.930 --> 28:09.930
You should stop that, Saigo-san.

28:09.930 --> 28:12.040
It's not nice to whine
and go back on your word.

28:12.480 --> 28:14.050
Pleasure to meet you.

28:14.560 --> 28:17.800
I'm Jirocho's daughter, Pirako Doromizu.

28:19.510 --> 28:20.900
Jirocho's...

28:21.380 --> 28:23.860
I have a question for you, Saigo-san.

28:23.860 --> 28:24.850
Do you have any

28:24.850 --> 28:27.640
proof that Otose-san
hasn't done anything?

28:27.850 --> 28:30.970
My proof is the fact
that you have no proof.

28:30.970 --> 28:34.650
Why would Otose pick
a fight with Jirocho?

28:34.860 --> 28:37.070
And now of all times?

28:37.290 --> 28:40.030
There's obviously a conspiracy going on.

28:40.290 --> 28:42.370
Nobody would spend that

28:42.370 --> 28:44.860
much effort to kill an old hag.

28:45.010 --> 28:46.310
Besides, we have proof

28:46.310 --> 28:48.540
that Otose-san would pick
a fight with my old man.

28:49.270 --> 28:52.790
There's a long history between them.

28:53.030 --> 28:54.790
Isn't that right, old man?

28:55.220 --> 28:56.710
Here it is.

28:56.710 --> 28:59.620
Otose-san's husband, Tatsugoro Terada,

28:59.620 --> 29:01.550
was killed by my old man.

29:04.270 --> 29:07.880
Oh? You didn't know?

29:08.070 --> 29:09.820
What about this?

29:10.270 --> 29:12.120
My old man and Tatsugoro-san

29:12.120 --> 29:14.440
were friends when they were young.

29:14.440 --> 29:18.320
But then they got into a
fight over a certain girl.

29:18.750 --> 29:21.160
Tatsugoro-san was the
one who won her over.

29:21.440 --> 29:24.880
I'm sure that my old man
wasn't happy about it.

29:24.880 --> 29:26.130
Stop it...

29:26.130 --> 29:28.430
That's why he killed his old friend.

29:28.430 --> 29:29.960
So he could have the girl.

29:30.390 --> 29:31.340
Stop it.

29:31.340 --> 29:34.070
Do you know why he abandoned his own

29:34.070 --> 29:36.840
wife and daughter to come to this town?

29:37.650 --> 29:41.770
That's because the girl,
Otose-san, is here.

29:43.530 --> 29:46.020
Didn't you hear me say to stop?

29:48.060 --> 29:50.520
See? It's just like I said.

29:50.520 --> 29:53.940
He cares more about Otose-san
than his own daughter.

29:54.240 --> 29:59.310
You came here just to tell me that?

29:59.440 --> 30:01.580
Such a dutiful daughter.

30:02.140 --> 30:03.730
If what I'm saying isn't true,

30:03.730 --> 30:06.280
that should mean you can kill Otose-san.

30:12.950 --> 30:14.420
Are you running away?!

30:15.310 --> 30:18.210
Saigo, don't worry.

30:18.210 --> 30:22.830
Yakuza don't need trannies
to clean up their mess.

30:23.360 --> 30:25.070
You stay out of it.

30:25.330 --> 30:27.480
I'll settle this myself.

30:27.480 --> 30:28.800
Wait!

30:28.800 --> 30:29.860
I'm not done talking...

30:30.140 --> 30:34.990
I'll spare you this one time,
since you kept whining.

30:35.290 --> 30:37.950
Could you shut up now?

30:38.180 --> 30:39.260
How am I supposed to shut u--

30:39.260 --> 30:40.950
Have you forgotten?

30:41.430 --> 30:43.160
If you go back on your word,

30:43.160 --> 30:45.450
we'll have to eliminate you as well.

30:45.990 --> 30:47.750
When laying siege to a castle,

30:47.750 --> 30:50.150
what would you target first?

30:50.390 --> 30:53.030
The weakest spot in the wall.

30:53.030 --> 30:55.960
A seasoned soldier like yourself
should be aware of this.

30:55.960 --> 30:57.970
M-Mama!

30:58.120 --> 31:00.970
Te-Teru-kun is... Teru-kun is...!

31:01.900 --> 31:04.580
Damn you!

31:05.000 --> 31:06.820
Snack Otose

31:05.950 --> 31:06.820
I see.

31:07.560 --> 31:08.820
Very well.

31:12.990 --> 31:14.170
Don't worry.

31:14.520 --> 31:15.660
That was Gintoki.

31:16.060 --> 31:17.890
It seems that Pirako is safe.

31:18.280 --> 31:20.340
They learned about the
new rule right before

31:20.340 --> 31:22.540
they were about to take
on Jirocho's gang.

31:22.740 --> 31:25.580
Apparently, they were able
to talk things through.

31:25.860 --> 31:27.160
That's a relief.

31:27.160 --> 31:29.170
I was worried that we would be too late.

31:29.170 --> 31:30.660
They kept us worried this whole time.

31:30.660 --> 31:32.340
What are they doing?!

31:32.720 --> 31:34.730
I appreciate everything you've done.

31:34.730 --> 31:36.980
You haven't eaten since
yesterday, right?

31:36.980 --> 31:39.450
Now that you mention it, I'm starting
to feel hungry now that everything's okay.

31:39.450 --> 31:40.520
Want to grab something to eat?

31:40.520 --> 31:41.350
Can we?

31:41.410 --> 31:42.430
Yakiniku!

31:42.430 --> 31:43.570
We must have yakiniku!

31:43.570 --> 31:44.540
At a really expensive place!

31:44.540 --> 31:45.260
Stupid!

31:45.260 --> 31:46.640
That won't fill my stomach!

31:46.640 --> 31:47.410
A buffet!

31:47.410 --> 31:48.890
At a place with ice cream!

31:48.890 --> 31:50.490
Stop fighting.

31:50.490 --> 31:52.610
Let's compromise by
going to a gas station.

31:52.610 --> 31:54.130
How is that a compromise?!

31:55.120 --> 31:56.850
Go on ahead.

31:56.850 --> 31:59.120
I'll join you once Gintoki
and Pirako are back.

32:00.080 --> 32:01.730
Please hurry.

32:01.730 --> 32:03.250
We'll wait for you
before we start eating.

32:03.250 --> 32:04.940
But the ice cream doesn't count, right?

32:04.940 --> 32:07.000
I can eat ice cream while
we're waiting, right?

32:11.190 --> 32:13.880
Didn't Otose-san seem a little strange?

32:14.140 --> 32:15.160
How?

32:15.160 --> 32:16.560
When she offers to buy someone dinner,

32:16.560 --> 32:18.640
there's usually a catch.

32:18.860 --> 32:20.970
No, that's not what I meant...

32:21.570 --> 32:22.390
Oh, sorry.

32:23.440 --> 32:24.700
He's covered in blood!

32:24.700 --> 32:25.420
Sorry!

32:25.420 --> 32:26.320
Is this my fault?!

32:26.320 --> 32:27.400
Is this my fault?!

32:27.700 --> 32:28.690
Huh?

32:28.690 --> 32:29.900
It's Katsuo-san...

32:29.900 --> 32:32.900
Hey! The bucket that
just ran past us...!

32:48.910 --> 32:51.040
Gran!

32:54.180 --> 33:00.190
Terada Family Grave

32:54.640 --> 32:57.190
It's rare to see you here.

32:57.990 --> 33:00.190
I'm assuming that you brought flowers.

33:00.860 --> 33:01.940
Hell no.

33:02.580 --> 33:06.700
Did you want me to bring
flowers for you, Otose?

33:07.150 --> 33:09.580
It's been years since
you've spoken to me,

33:09.580 --> 33:11.230
and that's all you have to say?

33:11.880 --> 33:14.200
You never change.

33:14.840 --> 33:18.640
If you lay me to rest
next to my husband,

33:18.640 --> 33:20.480
I suppose I can't complain.

33:20.890 --> 33:23.210
I heard that you took care of my kid.

33:24.090 --> 33:26.490
Save your thanks for that idiot.

33:26.760 --> 33:31.050
Though apparently, that
kid of yours got him good.

33:31.050 --> 33:33.490
She's quite a dutiful daughter.

33:33.830 --> 33:35.840
She came all the way here to clean

33:35.840 --> 33:37.740
this town for the sake of a

33:37.740 --> 33:39.600
stupid father who abandoned her.

33:39.860 --> 33:44.340
We've both been dancing to
the tune of a little kid.

33:44.720 --> 33:46.740
The years haven't been kind to us.

33:47.040 --> 33:50.370
Well, I suppose you knew
what was happening.

33:50.960 --> 33:52.550
The villain Jirocho

33:52.550 --> 33:55.870
can't go against the
daughter he left in tears?

33:57.830 --> 33:58.870
Otose...

33:59.080 --> 34:00.810
Get out of this town.

34:01.080 --> 34:03.410
This place will become
a battlefield very soon.

34:03.590 --> 34:07.200
It was gonna happen even if my
kid didn't rush things along.

34:07.570 --> 34:10.710
You'll only get in the way if you stay.

34:10.960 --> 34:15.020
So you were planning on
starting a war, period.

34:14.390 --> 34:19.640
Terada Family Grave

34:15.290 --> 34:16.470
I would have hoped that

34:16.470 --> 34:18.440
you wouldn't say those
words in his presence,

34:18.440 --> 34:19.640
even as a joke.

34:20.310 --> 34:22.460
Policeman and vigilante.

34:22.960 --> 34:25.820
The two of you were both
protecting this town,

34:25.820 --> 34:27.370
despite your different positions,

34:27.370 --> 34:29.700
but I suppose that was in the past.

34:32.550 --> 34:33.480
Jirocho.

34:33.970 --> 34:37.410
You went so far as to
abandon your wife and child

34:38.090 --> 34:39.890
so you could do this?

34:43.460 --> 34:45.560
Times have changed.

34:46.260 --> 34:49.630
A vigilante can't protect anything.

34:50.230 --> 34:54.000
He died and left you behind.

34:55.190 --> 34:58.040
Your methods are old-fashioned.

34:58.330 --> 35:00.080
You're just a nuisance,

35:00.080 --> 35:02.290
both you and Tatsugoro.

35:02.520 --> 35:04.830
This town doesn't need you anymore.

35:05.710 --> 35:09.330
This town belongs to me.

35:09.480 --> 35:11.420
I'll give you one more chance.

35:11.770 --> 35:13.460
Get out of this town.

35:18.750 --> 35:20.340
I have a favor to ask.

35:21.340 --> 35:24.340
They call me one of the Four Devas,

35:24.800 --> 35:28.140
but I don't have any
members in my faction.

35:28.140 --> 35:31.650
I'm sick of waiting for you to pay the rent. Take your fools and scram. Never come back to this town.
--Otose

35:29.010 --> 35:31.650
My life is all you need.

35:32.160 --> 35:35.440
They serve no use at all.

35:36.010 --> 35:38.790
They just happen to be my family.

35:41.920 --> 35:44.400
Is that your answer?

36:26.470 --> 36:28.470
You're Gintoki?

36:28.910 --> 36:30.610
You were a step too late.

36:30.920 --> 36:33.970
I buried her with her husband.

36:34.540 --> 36:36.980
Funny how it works.

36:37.470 --> 36:40.600
I believe that you were serving as her

36:40.600 --> 36:43.110
bodyguard to pay back a debt?

36:43.260 --> 36:46.490
That's over now. Your job is done.

36:47.910 --> 36:48.920
Scram.

36:48.920 --> 36:51.740
I'll spare your life for her sake.

36:56.960 --> 36:58.530
Ouch...

36:58.530 --> 37:00.500
The hell was that?

37:06.140 --> 37:08.220
Not bad, kid.

37:08.220 --> 37:09.970
You made me draw my sword.

37:11.160 --> 37:15.470
But are you willing to let Otose's
efforts to save your lives...

37:16.460 --> 37:18.270
...go to waste?

37:35.040 --> 37:37.160
You're not being very reasonable.

37:46.060 --> 37:47.340
It's over.

37:58.070 --> 38:02.630
I heard that Otose was keeping
a crazy monster around.

38:03.060 --> 38:04.780
So you're the White Yaksha?

38:04.980 --> 38:07.670
I never knew there was a freak like
you following in my footsteps.

38:08.300 --> 38:09.390
However...

38:09.590 --> 38:10.920
A generation managed

38:10.920 --> 38:13.890
to survive the brutal
battles of the Joi war.

38:14.180 --> 38:17.220
There were plenty more
like you out there.

38:18.880 --> 38:20.810
Get lost, watchdog.

38:21.110 --> 38:25.130
There's nothing for you to protect here.

38:58.750 --> 38:59.770
Hey, Gran.

39:00.480 --> 39:02.010
Are those manju?

39:02.570 --> 39:03.740
Can I have some?

39:04.220 --> 39:06.280
I'm starving to death here.

39:08.710 --> 39:10.710
These belong to my husband.

39:11.040 --> 39:12.280
Ask him.

39:18.200 --> 39:20.880
What did my husband say?

39:21.330 --> 39:22.660
Beats me.

39:22.660 --> 39:24.380
The dead don't talk.

39:24.580 --> 39:26.650
You're just asking for it.

39:26.980 --> 39:28.890
Don't blame me if you get cursed.

39:32.550 --> 39:35.930
The dead don't talk and
they don't eat dango.

39:36.220 --> 39:38.340
So I made a one-sided promise.

39:41.900 --> 39:43.720
I won't forget this debt.

39:44.090 --> 39:47.760
Your wife doesn't have
that much longer to live,

39:48.050 --> 39:53.170
but I'm going to protect
her in your stead.

40:08.960 --> 40:11.740
We appreciate your cooperation.

40:11.740 --> 40:17.280
It won't be long before the Jirocho gang and Lady Kada control the Kabuki district.

40:17.280 --> 40:19.030
Nonsense.

40:19.030 --> 40:23.380
You're merely using me to help your father take over the world.

40:23.380 --> 40:25.790
I could say the same about you, Lady Kada.

40:26.740 --> 40:32.410
As a result, the collar around my old man's neck has been released.

40:32.410 --> 40:36.100
That old hag took away the flowers and freedom my father once had.

40:36.100 --> 40:37.540
I'm sure that my old man will now...

40:37.540 --> 40:40.300
Pay more attention to you?

40:40.300 --> 40:46.310
I have a feeling that you're the one who can breathe easy now.

40:46.310 --> 40:50.590
You must be overjoyed to know that the woman who stole your father from you is dead.

40:50.590 --> 40:53.850
Man, this is why I hate women.

40:53.850 --> 40:56.110
They're always so suspicious.

40:56.110 --> 41:00.170
Anyway, I'll need you to take care of Saigo's kid.

41:00.170 --> 41:04.200
Who knows when that sheman will betray us?

41:04.200 --> 41:06.110
Pirako...

41:06.110 --> 41:10.150
Jirocho doesn't see you.

41:10.700 --> 41:13.170
You can eliminate every obstacle in the way.

41:13.170 --> 41:15.680
You can spend your entire life serving him.

41:15.680 --> 41:16.550
He will never turn to you...

41:16.550 --> 41:17.370
Man...

41:17.370 --> 41:20.260
Could you cut it out, Lady Kada?

41:20.660 --> 41:26.380
If you don't shut your mouth, I'll have to make some flowers, you hag.

41:30.970 --> 41:32.980
Greater Edo Hospital

41:39.330 --> 41:42.410
Madame Catherine, you should get some rest.

41:42.410 --> 41:44.670
You have been standing there for two days.

41:44.670 --> 41:47.010
I do not require any rest.

41:47.010 --> 41:49.080
Shall I take your place, Madame Catherine?

41:49.960 --> 41:52.110
Kagura-chan, shouldn't you get some rest too?

41:52.110 --> 41:55.760
I'm not skanky enough to go to sleep in someone else's house.

41:55.760 --> 41:57.160
Besides...

41:57.160 --> 41:59.840
What if I wake up to find out she's...

42:00.410 --> 42:01.950
She'll be fine.

42:01.950 --> 42:03.360
I'm sure she'll be fine.

42:03.360 --> 42:05.520
You should go home and get some rest.

42:05.910 --> 42:09.220
She would be upset if she learned that everyone was ruining their health.

42:09.220 --> 42:12.190
You have no home to return to.

42:12.190 --> 42:15.270
There's no place for you here.

42:15.270 --> 42:16.410
Saigo-san!

42:16.410 --> 42:18.150
That fool.

42:18.150 --> 42:20.440
I kept telling her to escape...

42:20.440 --> 42:22.000
Saigo-san...

42:22.000 --> 42:23.360
Was that phone call...?

42:24.030 --> 42:27.290
I'm not going to apologize.

42:27.290 --> 42:29.040
There was nothing I could do.

42:29.040 --> 42:31.030
And there's nothing I can do now.

42:31.830 --> 42:33.520
The day after tomorrow...

42:32.920 --> 42:38.970
Odd Jobs Gin-chan
Snack Otose

42:33.520 --> 42:38.650
Your place will be destroyed by the Four Devas.

42:39.570 --> 42:41.150
The day after tomorrow.

42:41.150 --> 42:44.560
You have until then to pack up and leave this town.

42:44.560 --> 42:46.740
Wh-Why is this happening?!

42:46.740 --> 42:48.380
Didn't you hear me?

42:48.380 --> 42:51.380
There's no place for you here in this town.

42:51.380 --> 42:55.730
The entire Kabuki district is against you.

42:55.730 --> 42:57.790
Did they take your kid hostage?

42:57.990 --> 42:59.290
Gin-san...

42:59.290 --> 43:02.930
They appear to be testing me.

43:02.930 --> 43:07.630
There are things I'll do anything to protect.

43:07.630 --> 43:09.000
Saigo-san...

43:09.000 --> 43:12.570
Pako, can you take care of them?

43:12.570 --> 43:14.270
Don't worry.

43:14.270 --> 43:16.850
I'm closing up shop.

43:16.850 --> 43:19.110
The rest is up to you.

43:19.110 --> 43:20.610
You bastard!

43:20.610 --> 43:22.310
Otose-san was left for dead!

43:22.310 --> 43:23.880
Her bar was destroyed!

43:23.880 --> 43:26.120
And you're just gonna turn tail and run?!

43:26.120 --> 43:27.840
You're telling me to fight?

43:27.840 --> 43:29.330
Don't make me laugh.

43:29.330 --> 43:31.370
I couldn't even take Jirocho one-on-one.

43:31.370 --> 43:33.480
When did you become so pathetic?!

43:33.480 --> 43:35.370
Damn you, Sakata!

43:35.370 --> 43:37.970
If you're gonna leave, you can leave by yourself!

43:37.970 --> 43:40.290
I won't! I won't...!

43:40.290 --> 43:43.180
Do you know why Gran went by herself?

43:43.590 --> 43:46.350
To protect us.

43:46.350 --> 43:48.070
If you still insist on dying,

43:48.070 --> 43:50.450
you're free to stay behind and get yourself killed.

43:50.450 --> 43:53.660
Odd Jobs and Gran's bar are being closed down.

43:53.660 --> 43:55.640
We're just strangers now.

43:56.210 --> 43:58.500
Free to do as we please.

43:58.500 --> 44:00.530
I'll be doing just that.

44:00.530 --> 44:01.290
Wait!

44:01.290 --> 44:02.510
Gin-san!

44:02.510 --> 44:04.320
Sorry.

44:05.210 --> 44:09.160
I doubt I can protect anything now...

44:10.300 --> 44:11.830
Gin-san...

44:12.920 --> 44:14.460
Master Gintoki...

44:17.910 --> 44:21.290
Kabuki District 1st Street

44:19.110 --> 44:21.820
Doesn't it feel like there aren't many people around these days?

44:21.820 --> 44:23.380
Didn't you know?

44:23.380 --> 44:25.760
There's a war brewing around these parts.

44:25.760 --> 44:26.550
A war?

44:26.550 --> 44:30.480
The factional rivalry between the Four Devas is heating up.

44:30.480 --> 44:32.890
Everybody's too scared to come near this town.

44:33.150 --> 44:34.900
Is it really that dangerous?

44:34.900 --> 44:36.830
We've managed to survive everything that's come before.

44:36.830 --> 44:37.680
This is no different.

44:37.680 --> 44:40.940
Puppet House

44:37.950 --> 44:40.940
But there are rumors that Otose's dead.

44:40.940 --> 44:41.930
What?!

44:41.930 --> 44:44.080
She got in a fight with Jirocho's gang.

44:44.080 --> 44:47.690
And it sounds like Katsuo, one of their young leaders, also died.

44:47.690 --> 44:52.900
But there's this rookie who's filling in for Katsuo.

44:52.900 --> 44:57.200
I heard that she persuaded Kada and Saigo to help crush Otose-san.

44:57.470 --> 45:01.520
I still owe her for lending me money when I was in debt.

45:01.520 --> 45:04.840
I owe her for helping me out when I got in a fight with my wife.

45:04.840 --> 45:08.070
Why don't you go protect Otose-san's bar then?

45:08.070 --> 45:10.720
Don't be stupid. I'd be throwing my life away.

45:10.720 --> 45:15.510
In this town, the wicked live longer than the kind.

45:15.510 --> 45:18.210
Who knows when the three remaining Devas will turn on one another...

45:18.210 --> 45:21.850
It's probably time to get out of this town.

45:22.360 --> 45:28.360
Odd Jobs Gin-chan
Snack Otose

45:24.810 --> 45:28.880
The Kabuki District, a town which accepts the clean and unclean.

45:28.880 --> 45:34.860
I was unable to predict that we would be chased out of this town.

45:35.240 --> 45:39.460
Madame Otose loved this town of good and evil.

45:39.960 --> 45:41.790
But now, we can never...

45:41.790 --> 45:46.950
Why must we abandon Otose's bar? Our bar...

45:46.950 --> 45:49.150
Don't say that.

45:50.060 --> 45:55.050
If we die, Otose-san will have risked her life for nothing.

45:55.050 --> 45:59.130
Otose-san will be moved out of the Kabuki district hospital tomorrow.

45:59.130 --> 46:02.170
We'll be able to visit her every day.

46:02.170 --> 46:05.630
Anyway, we'll have to stay away from the Kabuki district.

46:05.630 --> 46:09.420
As long as we're alive, we can always start...

46:11.840 --> 46:13.550
Start over...

46:13.840 --> 46:15.970
S-Start...

46:18.330 --> 46:20.920
Huh? That's strange...

46:22.520 --> 46:25.040
Why am I crying?

46:25.490 --> 46:26.760
Huh?

46:41.210 --> 46:45.210
So you couldn't take on the Four Devas.

46:45.210 --> 46:50.850
I didn't think our boss would actually attack Otose.

46:50.850 --> 46:56.110
You probably thought you could calm things down by saving my life, but tough luck.

46:56.110 --> 46:58.230
Nobody can stop this war.

47:00.900 --> 47:02.340
Don't get the wrong idea.

47:03.040 --> 47:05.580
I wasn't trying to save your life.

47:05.580 --> 47:07.920
I just needed you to spill your guts.

47:07.920 --> 47:09.340
Let's get those guts out of you.

47:09.750 --> 47:11.890
What?! What do you wanna know?!

47:11.890 --> 47:15.540
Why were you surprised that Jirocho attacked Gran?

47:16.480 --> 47:18.290
You didn't know?

47:18.290 --> 47:21.650
The boss and Otose have known each other since they were kids.

47:21.650 --> 47:22.750
You could say they were childhood friends.

47:23.130 --> 47:25.710
The boss was a pretty naughty kid,

47:25.710 --> 47:29.980
but Otose was there to straighten him out every time he tried something.

47:30.650 --> 47:36.970
As a result, the boss became a vigilante who was popular enough to be considered a leader of the town.

47:36.970 --> 47:41.190
Jirocho, man among men, would never have existed without Otose.

47:41.620 --> 47:44.810
At the time, nobody could defeat the boss in a fight.

47:44.810 --> 47:50.300
But, there was one man who managed to triumph over the boss once.

47:50.880 --> 47:54.910
Tatsugoro Terada, a cop who was also a leader of the town

47:54.910 --> 47:56.780
and Otose's husband.

47:57.340 --> 48:01.380
A man who was strong in a fight and stuck to his ideals.

48:01.380 --> 48:04.090
Everyone had to love him.

48:04.500 --> 48:06.520
Cop and vigilante.

48:06.520 --> 48:09.450
They got in a fight once because of their different positions,

48:09.450 --> 48:12.390
but they both fought to protect their town.

48:12.390 --> 48:16.330
It wasn't long before they became friends.

48:16.730 --> 48:19.120
But there was one problem.

48:19.120 --> 48:23.360
They were in love with the same woman.

48:24.280 --> 48:29.030
The boss backed down because he wanted Otose to be happy,

48:29.030 --> 48:32.790
since he figured a vigilante wouldn't be able to provide that happiness.

48:33.680 --> 48:38.040
But Tatsugoro got himself killed, which left Otose alone.

48:38.600 --> 48:41.170
And he died in the middle of a battle,

48:41.430 --> 48:43.650
taking a bullet that was meant for the boss.

48:45.050 --> 48:49.430
Doromizu Gang

48:45.050 --> 48:52.060
When the boss returned from the war, his wife and daughter were waiting for him.

48:52.770 --> 48:56.660
But the boss paid no attention to his daughter.

48:56.660 --> 49:01.150
He was willing to do anything, no matter how underhanded it was, for the sake of business.

49:01.640 --> 49:07.950
He said that he didn't have the right to be a father or a vigilante.

49:07.950 --> 49:13.910
Who was it, what was it, that drove the boss to give up all he had to stay in this town?

49:14.240 --> 49:18.760
Now that he's struck down the old lady, I'm not really sure.

49:19.250 --> 49:21.390
But was this really the right thing to do?

49:22.470 --> 49:25.950
Will this really make them happy?

49:27.250 --> 49:30.000
They're never gonna be happy...

49:30.010 --> 49:31.940
...'cause I'm gonna crush them.

49:31.940 --> 49:34.680
So you were putting on a show for the kids.

49:34.680 --> 49:36.420
You don't stand a chance by yourself.

49:37.110 --> 49:40.170
I can't go back on my word.

49:40.460 --> 49:42.550
Joe Schmo, take care of Gran.

49:42.550 --> 49:43.720
What?! Why?!

49:43.720 --> 49:46.390
You always return the favor, seven for three.

49:47.090 --> 49:54.560
Shouldn't you stay here to watch this old woman pass on?

49:55.140 --> 49:56.620
Gintoki...

49:56.930 --> 50:00.470
I don't want to see...

50:00.470 --> 50:02.580
...you die.

50:06.020 --> 50:09.880
Gran, I promise to pay off the rent.

50:09.880 --> 50:12.110
So sit tight.

50:14.550 --> 50:18.410
How did it feel to cut down the woman you loved?

50:20.430 --> 50:25.070
How did it feel to manipulate a bunch of old men and women?

50:25.070 --> 50:27.160
That's harsh.

50:27.160 --> 50:30.470
I did it all for your sake.

50:30.470 --> 50:34.900
Next, you'll have Saigo destroy Otose's bar.

50:34.900 --> 50:37.040
What a waste of time...

50:37.040 --> 50:39.730
Did that vixen put you up to it?

50:39.960 --> 50:42.190
Of course not.

50:42.190 --> 50:44.240
This is part of the plan.

50:44.240 --> 50:48.580
There are many people left in this town who were involved with Otose.

50:48.580 --> 50:51.610
We'll use this chance to flush them out.

50:51.610 --> 50:53.400
Saigo happens to be one of them.

50:53.400 --> 50:56.690
Will it really work?

50:57.250 --> 51:04.130
And you don't need to worry. The old woman's buddies aren't in this town anymore.

51:04.130 --> 51:07.130
The watchdog's chains have been snapped.

51:07.690 --> 51:12.590
You intend to keep your promise to not harm anyone else?

51:12.590 --> 51:14.370
It's no use.

51:14.370 --> 51:17.810
That person was never chained.

51:18.000 --> 51:22.500
You took him to be an obedient dog who could be chained?

51:23.940 --> 51:26.360
I guarantee that Bro will come.

51:27.040 --> 51:30.210
You were watching?

51:30.180 --> 51:31.850
I was watching.

51:31.850 --> 51:34.520
When you failed to finish off Otose too...

51:34.810 --> 51:39.860
When you cut her down so she wouldn't be dragged into this war...

51:40.970 --> 51:42.930
I figured it out.

51:42.930 --> 51:46.090
You're just like him.

51:46.400 --> 51:50.530
But I'm going to protect her in your stead.

51:52.300 --> 51:53.810
Jirocho...

51:53.820 --> 51:58.450
Take care of her... Take care of our town...

51:59.130 --> 52:02.940
Both of you are chained to this town by the same thing.

52:02.940 --> 52:06.950
A promise made to a certain man.

52:07.270 --> 52:10.020
An iron vow of your own choosing.

52:10.530 --> 52:12.360
The chains of a warrior.

52:13.020 --> 52:16.880
Both of you are animals bound by the same chain.

52:17.330 --> 52:18.610
But...

52:18.610 --> 52:26.330
One has experienced loss, but accepted the responsibility and continues to protect this town.

52:26.330 --> 52:28.530
The other has experienced loss,

52:28.530 --> 52:35.300
but has abandoned the responsibility and chosen to protect this town by using force to conquer it.

52:35.320 --> 52:40.370
Two beasts whose interests clash, despite sharing the same goal.

52:40.380 --> 52:44.300
Now, who will be the last man standing over the Kabuki district?

52:46.160 --> 52:48.300
Don't worry.

52:48.300 --> 52:50.810
I've already made up my mind.

52:51.080 --> 52:53.930
I'll be joining you on your rampage.

52:54.830 --> 52:58.820
I promise to help you take over this town.

52:59.210 --> 53:02.830
So once this is finished,

53:03.390 --> 53:07.740
you'll come back to me, won't you?

53:10.210 --> 53:11.850
You...

53:18.640 --> 53:20.440
Where do you think you're going?

53:21.420 --> 53:24.240
With Otose-san's mementos of her husband...

53:24.240 --> 53:26.440
Why are you here?

53:26.440 --> 53:29.930
You're the one who said we could do as we please.

53:29.930 --> 53:31.700
Take us with you.

53:31.930 --> 53:33.510
We can help you fight.

53:34.270 --> 53:35.870
Don't get the wrong idea.

53:36.070 --> 53:39.390
I'm just here because Gran told me to pick this up for her.

53:39.930 --> 53:41.740
Enough already...

53:41.740 --> 53:44.140
Neither of you get it...

53:44.720 --> 53:48.860
If you shoulder the burden alone and leave us behind...

53:48.860 --> 53:51.850
How are we supposed to be happy you saved our lives?

53:52.310 --> 53:56.850
How are we supposed to be happy that Gran saved us if she's gone?

53:57.230 --> 54:02.860
If you're gone, life won't be any fun!

54:04.960 --> 54:07.380
Life doesn't need to be fun.

54:08.110 --> 54:12.370
I just want you to live.

54:12.910 --> 54:16.250
I don't want to go through that again.

54:16.960 --> 54:20.420
I don't want anyone to die.

54:23.630 --> 54:27.090
Aren't you supposed to be Gintoki Sakata?

54:27.090 --> 54:30.800
The man who's let so much slip away, who's failed to protect so much...

54:30.810 --> 54:33.180
...but swore that he would never run away from his responsibilities!

54:33.180 --> 54:35.530
Didn't you promise her husband?!

54:35.530 --> 54:38.700
Once you've decided to protect something, you'll protect it to the very end!

54:38.700 --> 54:41.240
Isn't that what makes you Gintoki Sakata?!

54:41.240 --> 54:44.650
So what if Otose-san's life was in danger?!

54:44.650 --> 54:46.770
This isn't enough to kill Otose-san off!

54:46.770 --> 54:47.960
Isn't enough to kill us off!

54:47.960 --> 54:49.590
Isn't enough to kill you off!

54:49.590 --> 54:53.000
Because you're going to protect us!

54:53.000 --> 54:56.500
Because we're going to protect you!

54:58.600 --> 55:00.760
Isn't that what Odd Jobs is about?

55:01.200 --> 55:06.860
Isn't that how the three of us protected so much over the years?

55:09.010 --> 55:13.150
We have not lost anything yet.

55:13.150 --> 55:17.550
So you must not lose your soul.

55:17.530 --> 55:20.150
Catherine-san, Tama-san...

55:20.170 --> 55:21.280
Master Gintoki...

55:21.790 --> 55:25.780
You have protected us many times.

55:25.990 --> 55:29.620
No matter how dire or hopeless the situation was...

55:29.620 --> 55:31.930
We trust you.

55:31.930 --> 55:35.170
So it's your turn to trust us.

55:35.720 --> 55:37.530
We can do this together.

55:37.530 --> 55:41.220
We can protect Otose-san's home, our home.

55:40.420 --> 55:45.180
Kabuki District 1st Street

55:41.220 --> 55:45.860
Protect the town which brought us together.

55:49.560 --> 55:51.350
Sorry, pops.

55:52.070 --> 55:54.510
I bought these for you,

55:54.510 --> 55:56.940
but there probably won't be any left over.

55:57.690 --> 56:00.780
In return, I'll make another promise.

56:01.580 --> 56:06.120
We promise to protect everything which was dear to you.

56:12.390 --> 56:14.390
Thanks, pops,

56:14.770 --> 56:17.940
for leading me to these assholes.

56:23.650 --> 56:28.850
What's with that group of men or women or both or neither?

56:28.850 --> 56:31.270
It's the Jirocho's gang and Saigo's people!

56:31.270 --> 56:33.160
Th-There's gonna be a war!

56:33.410 --> 56:35.120
Why is this happening?

56:35.110 --> 56:37.250
Don't say anything.

56:37.250 --> 56:40.000
Mama's the one who's hurting the most.

56:41.670 --> 56:42.460
Odd Jobs Gin-chan

56:42.460 --> 56:44.920
Odd Jobs Gin-chan
Snack Otose

56:44.920 --> 56:47.730
Let's get started then!

56:47.770 --> 56:50.890
Make a lot of noise for Otose!

56:50.890 --> 56:52.600
Wait, young lady!

56:52.600 --> 56:54.200
The store banner is up!

56:52.600 --> 56:54.480
Otose

56:54.480 --> 56:56.220
H-How can this be?!

56:56.220 --> 56:57.830
Th-This early in the morning?!

56:57.830 --> 56:59.390
They work too hard!

56:59.390 --> 57:00.110
You're missing the point!

57:00.440 --> 57:03.520
Why is the store banner up when Otose and everyone else is...?

57:04.760 --> 57:06.360
Could it be...

57:07.050 --> 57:08.970
Y-You're...!

57:10.120 --> 57:12.490
Sorry, but could you come back later?

57:12.490 --> 57:14.530
The place is booked.

57:14.530 --> 57:17.010
I feel like drinking by myself.

57:17.010 --> 57:19.000
Without any interruptions.

57:19.250 --> 57:19.580
What are you...?

57:19.570 --> 57:23.670
Don't come any closer.

57:23.670 --> 57:26.020
The hell are you talking about?!

57:30.800 --> 57:32.370
Didn't you hear me?

57:33.160 --> 57:38.650
I told you to keep your stinkin' pig feet out of this place.

57:38.650 --> 57:39.980
Pako!

57:40.410 --> 57:43.150
I knew you would come, Bro.

57:43.360 --> 57:44.200
Eh?!

57:44.190 --> 57:48.410
You're gonna take on the entire Kabuki District?!

57:48.210 --> 57:50.010
The entire Kabuki District?

57:50.010 --> 57:51.380
Don't make me laugh.

57:51.380 --> 57:54.300
You fools aren't even part of this town.

57:54.300 --> 57:57.720
You're no different from the dogshit on the side of the road.

57:58.090 --> 58:03.560
All I need from the Kabuki District is right here.

58:03.880 --> 58:06.140
Our Kabuki District...

58:06.470 --> 58:07.890
...can be found...

58:08.260 --> 58:09.850
...right here.

58:10.060 --> 58:12.340
Crush us if you can.

58:12.340 --> 58:15.540
We're not letting any of you into our town.

58:15.540 --> 58:16.840
Pako!

58:16.840 --> 58:18.440
Please stop this!

58:18.440 --> 58:20.980
We don't want to fight you!

58:20.980 --> 58:22.590
Funny.

58:22.590 --> 58:24.270
It's very strange.

58:24.270 --> 58:28.320
It makes me sick to have to fight friends.

58:28.320 --> 58:33.000
Yet I felt relieved when I saw your face.

58:33.900 --> 58:35.280
Of course.

58:35.280 --> 58:38.210
It wouldn't be right if you weren't here.

58:38.210 --> 58:39.290
What are you...?

58:39.300 --> 58:43.280
Assmi, it would be rude to say anything.

58:43.280 --> 58:44.550
That's right!

58:44.550 --> 58:46.470
There's nothing left to say.

58:46.470 --> 58:53.060
Bro and Saigo-san are both protecting what's dear to them.

58:53.760 --> 58:56.160
You shouldn't be talking.

58:56.160 --> 58:59.640
Not when you're the one who took what was dear to me.

58:59.890 --> 59:03.640
I'm not going to apologize. After all...

59:04.640 --> 59:07.650
I'm here to protect what's dear to me.

59:08.030 --> 59:11.770
I'll steal and destroy what's dear to others...

59:11.770 --> 59:15.060
...if that's what's needed to take him back.

59:15.060 --> 59:19.440
I must pity you, daughter of Jirocho.

59:21.140 --> 59:25.100
The swing of a samurai's blade can silence a thousand words!

59:27.000 --> 59:28.710
Warriors,

59:28.710 --> 59:32.340
let us hold our conversation in a whirlwind of blood!

59:34.550 --> 59:39.720
The Otose Family will be paying our respects.

59:39.720 --> 59:42.860
Let's go, bastards!

01:00:00.490 --> 01:00:02.260
Shifting to cleaning mode.

01:00:02.700 --> 01:00:05.670
I will not stop until I have
eliminated all of the trash

01:00:05.670 --> 01:00:07.270
in the Kabuki district.

01:00:08.160 --> 01:00:09.660
It's cleaning time.

01:00:22.130 --> 01:00:23.060
What's with them?!

01:00:23.580 --> 01:00:26.540
They're like little demons!

01:00:28.410 --> 01:00:30.020
Who are they?!

01:00:30.020 --> 01:00:33.130
Why are these monsters
working for that old hag?!

01:00:30.080 --> 01:00:33.130
Odd Jobs Gin-chan
Snack Otose

01:00:33.360 --> 01:00:34.850
You could say that Otose

01:00:34.850 --> 01:00:36.880
has the power to attract such people.

01:00:37.510 --> 01:00:38.780
We have no choice then.

01:00:38.780 --> 01:00:39.880
Time to get serious.

01:00:42.610 --> 01:00:43.550
Saigo!

01:00:45.120 --> 01:00:47.260
Too bad, Bro.

01:00:47.580 --> 01:00:50.600
You were trying to buy time
by fighting a bunch of chumps,

01:00:50.600 --> 01:00:53.020
but that cat burglar of
yours won't be coming back.

01:00:53.290 --> 01:00:57.270
She won't be able to steal Saigo's son.

01:00:57.850 --> 01:01:01.280
Even if she manages to
make it to Teruhiko-kun,

01:01:01.280 --> 01:01:04.330
Kada's people and my old
man will be waiting.

01:01:04.330 --> 01:01:06.500
It's pretty much impossible for her

01:01:06.500 --> 01:01:07.910
to make it back alive.

01:01:07.910 --> 01:01:10.750
That's what you were trying to do...

01:01:11.190 --> 01:01:14.540
There's no point in trying to
avoid a fight with Saigo-san.

01:01:14.540 --> 01:01:16.380
Look what will happen
if you take too long.

01:01:16.380 --> 01:01:19.380
Odd Jobs Gin-chan

01:01:16.740 --> 01:01:19.380
Otose-san's bar is going to burn down.

01:01:19.870 --> 01:01:20.780
The building's on fire!

01:01:20.780 --> 01:01:21.550
Oh, no!

01:01:21.550 --> 01:01:22.560
We have to put it out!

01:01:22.560 --> 01:01:23.720
You're leaving?

01:01:23.720 --> 01:01:26.370
I believe that you barely have
enough fighters as it is.

01:01:27.980 --> 01:01:31.230
You're pretty brutal
for a little shrimp.

01:01:32.040 --> 01:01:34.680
I'm starting to like you.

01:01:35.010 --> 01:01:38.810
But I'll need to separate your
head from your body first.

01:01:38.810 --> 01:01:41.690
I've always liked you, Bro.

01:01:42.060 --> 01:01:44.690
But you have to join my old man first.

01:01:45.150 --> 01:01:48.560
Actually, you should just marry me.

01:01:48.560 --> 01:01:51.700
That's the only way for you
to survive in this town.

01:01:52.160 --> 01:01:55.700
You guys are all alone
with no coming to help.

01:01:59.370 --> 01:02:01.450
All alone with no help?

01:02:01.810 --> 01:02:03.080
I don't think so.

01:02:03.790 --> 01:02:07.210
At least, there's one person
here who's willing to help.

01:02:07.430 --> 01:02:08.900
Yeah, Gin-san?

01:02:08.900 --> 01:02:09.460
You're...

01:02:10.290 --> 01:02:11.290
...Tatsumi the firefighter!

01:02:11.880 --> 01:02:13.060
Who are you?!

01:02:13.060 --> 01:02:13.890
Trying to interfere?!

01:02:13.890 --> 01:02:15.410
Die!

01:02:16.210 --> 01:02:17.910
That's some weak iron.

01:02:18.430 --> 01:02:22.160
You can't even scratch
these guys with that junk.

01:02:22.630 --> 01:02:24.550
Want me to reforge that for you?

01:02:26.090 --> 01:02:27.200
Te-Tetsuko!

01:02:27.490 --> 01:02:29.250
Don't take us lightly!

01:02:29.500 --> 01:02:30.800
Hey, now.

01:02:30.800 --> 01:02:34.260
A lady doesn't like it
when you gang up on her.

01:02:36.490 --> 01:02:41.060
Yes, a man should be hard-boiled, Camus

01:02:41.350 --> 01:02:43.060
Kozenigata-san! Haji-san!

01:02:42.690 --> 01:02:45.310
What's with that weird-looking bunch?!

01:02:46.210 --> 01:02:47.440
Master Gengai!

01:02:47.740 --> 01:02:50.200
Hey! There's a freak mixed in there!

01:02:50.200 --> 01:02:52.070
Can't let this bar be shut down!

01:02:53.090 --> 01:02:54.700
No more free drinks for me!

01:02:54.840 --> 01:02:55.770
You have a running tab.

01:02:55.770 --> 01:02:57.330
Why am I the only one who
gets the cold shoulder?!

01:02:59.380 --> 01:03:04.200
The Members of Odd Jobs, you are not alone.

01:03:04.200 --> 01:03:07.340
They have forged a bond during
their time in this town.

01:03:07.500 --> 01:03:10.160
What?! Now we have an
army of male escorts!

01:03:10.160 --> 01:03:14.220
The Kabuki district women
may cry once I'm gone.

01:03:14.220 --> 01:03:17.600
But I will cry once you're gone.

01:03:19.060 --> 01:03:23.710
How very naughty of you
to seduce a male escort.

01:03:23.710 --> 01:03:24.850
Kyoshiro-san!

01:03:26.410 --> 01:03:28.960
We won't let you carry the burden alone.

01:03:28.960 --> 01:03:30.480
And here are a bunch of cabaret girls!

01:03:30.480 --> 01:03:33.310
It's not very nice to decide the fate of

01:03:33.310 --> 01:03:35.020
the Kabuki district on your own.

01:03:35.500 --> 01:03:37.870
This town doesn't belong to any of you.

01:03:37.870 --> 01:03:42.000
It belongs to us cabaret girls.

01:03:42.000 --> 01:03:45.630
The Jirocho gang and tranny
gang can bring it on.

01:03:45.630 --> 01:03:48.120
We'll show you how terrifying

01:03:48.120 --> 01:03:50.500
the Kabuki district truly is.

01:03:50.570 --> 01:03:52.220
What's with these people?!

01:03:52.220 --> 01:03:55.690
Young lady, they
completely outnumber us!

01:03:56.880 --> 01:04:00.280
Is that supposed to matter?

01:04:00.280 --> 01:04:01.800
We're up against a bunch of amateurs!

01:04:01.800 --> 01:04:03.610
Take them all out!

01:04:03.610 --> 01:04:04.440
Yeah!

01:04:04.440 --> 01:04:07.200
We can't let a bunch of
cabaret girls boss us around!

01:04:09.530 --> 01:04:11.910
A bunch of cabaret girls, you said?

01:04:12.520 --> 01:04:14.090
Get down on your knees.

01:04:14.590 --> 01:04:16.920
I am the queen of the Kabuki district.

01:04:20.380 --> 01:04:21.290
Idiot!

01:04:21.290 --> 01:04:24.550
Are you trying to protect
this town or destroy it?!

01:04:25.000 --> 01:04:27.090
Don't forget that you
have allies down here!

01:04:27.090 --> 01:04:28.800
Straighten out your act or
I'll have to punish you!

01:04:29.260 --> 01:04:31.700
If the town gets destroyed,
we can rebuild it.

01:04:31.700 --> 01:04:33.640
This time, we can build
a sturdy iron town.

01:04:33.640 --> 01:04:35.270
What are you talking about?

01:04:35.660 --> 01:04:39.650
We already live in an iron town.

01:04:39.650 --> 01:04:42.150
Gin-san, you guys go
settle this business!

01:04:42.150 --> 01:04:44.350
We'll handle the small fry here!

01:04:43.850 --> 01:04:45.150
You're the small fry!

01:04:55.110 --> 01:04:58.760
That's the difference between you,
who takes things that others hold dear,

01:04:58.760 --> 01:05:02.130
and them, who protect the
things that others hold dear.

01:05:02.370 --> 01:05:06.720
You should know when a
battle is lost, Saigo-san.

01:05:07.220 --> 01:05:08.420
Leave.

01:05:08.420 --> 01:05:09.970
This battle is our...

01:05:10.780 --> 01:05:12.470
...Gran's victory.

01:05:12.590 --> 01:05:15.140
As long as Saigo-san and I are here,

01:05:15.140 --> 01:05:18.500
your crowd doesn't stand a chance.

01:05:18.500 --> 01:05:20.600
I won't let you go to my old man.

01:05:20.870 --> 01:05:22.230
I said that you already lost.

01:05:22.650 --> 01:05:25.230
You've really pissed them off.

01:05:26.030 --> 01:05:28.570
Stay out of this, curly head!

01:05:28.770 --> 01:05:30.470
I'm disappointed, Pako.

01:05:30.470 --> 01:05:33.200
You're going to let a couple
of kids throw their lives away?

01:05:33.200 --> 01:05:34.760
So be it.

01:05:34.760 --> 01:05:37.080
I'd rather disappoint you
than disappoint them.

01:05:38.560 --> 01:05:40.600
A couple of softies who
didn't want to fight

01:05:40.600 --> 01:05:43.170
Saigo-san are supposed to put up a fight?

01:05:43.490 --> 01:05:46.920
Looks like I'll need to rip your
head off to make you understand.

01:05:47.130 --> 01:05:52.680
True, we were softies
who let you use us.

01:05:53.500 --> 01:05:55.410
You tricked us, betrayed us,

01:05:55.410 --> 01:05:58.820
but we'll be able to laugh
it off in a couple of days.

01:05:59.180 --> 01:06:01.730
I'm used to having girls trick me.

01:06:02.380 --> 01:06:05.480
But, no matter your reasons...

01:06:07.300 --> 01:06:11.660
We can never forgive you for hurting...

01:06:11.990 --> 01:06:13.160
...the Kabuki district's mother.

01:06:13.760 --> 01:06:15.510
Don't underestimate Odd Jobs.

01:06:15.890 --> 01:06:17.840
We won't let you hurt anyone else.

01:06:17.840 --> 01:06:20.100
You won't have your way around here.

01:06:20.100 --> 01:06:22.100
We aren't alone!

01:06:22.100 --> 01:06:24.660
Now that the three members
of Odd Jobs are together,

01:06:24.660 --> 01:06:28.560
you won't be taking
anything else from us!

01:06:28.560 --> 01:06:31.230
It's time to show you the power...

01:06:31.800 --> 01:06:33.200
...that has kept Odd Jobs safe.

01:06:33.230 --> 01:06:34.850
It would be rude to go easy

01:06:34.850 --> 01:06:37.210
on someone with such fierce eyes.

01:06:37.210 --> 01:06:39.020
I understand.

01:06:39.020 --> 01:06:42.470
Then I'll turn you into corpses first.

01:06:43.000 --> 01:06:46.510
Where would you like me to
make some bright red flowers?

01:06:46.510 --> 01:06:47.980
Your head?

01:06:47.980 --> 01:06:49.230
Or your chest?

01:06:49.230 --> 01:06:50.230
Or...

01:06:53.750 --> 01:06:56.320
...Bro's heart?

01:07:01.950 --> 01:07:04.330
There won't be any flowers.

01:07:08.090 --> 01:07:10.830
Flowers aren't for samurai.

01:07:18.440 --> 01:07:22.760
Flowers are meant for girls.

01:07:22.780 --> 01:07:24.480
And trannies.

01:07:24.560 --> 01:07:26.400
Huh...

01:07:26.400 --> 01:07:28.290
That's strange...

01:07:28.290 --> 01:07:32.380
How could I...

01:07:33.900 --> 01:07:40.370
I can't let them reach my old man.

01:07:40.370 --> 01:07:43.260
I'm gonna...

01:07:46.550 --> 01:07:47.990
You used the back of your blade?

01:07:47.990 --> 01:07:49.970
You're still softies.

01:07:50.550 --> 01:07:53.510
You hit my chin so hard
that my head's spinning.

01:07:53.510 --> 01:07:56.230
I won't be able to stand anytime soon.

01:07:56.730 --> 01:08:00.440
Damn. Guess I can't stop you.

01:08:01.110 --> 01:08:02.730
You're just as soft.

01:08:03.180 --> 01:08:05.650
Yeah, I'm gonna talk
to myself for a bit.

01:08:05.650 --> 01:08:07.240
Don't pay any attention.

01:08:07.240 --> 01:08:09.620
We'll take care of your kid.

01:08:09.620 --> 01:08:12.700
Rest easy and get some
beauty sleep or ugly sleep.

01:08:13.720 --> 01:08:16.370
Then I'll also talk to myself for a bit.

01:08:17.090 --> 01:08:19.360
Don't get yourselves killed.

01:08:22.350 --> 01:08:23.960
I leave the Kabuki district,

01:08:24.240 --> 01:08:28.440
our town, in your hands, Odd Jobs.

01:08:29.840 --> 01:08:34.590
This town looks pretty meek
when there's nobody around.

01:08:34.940 --> 01:08:36.690
Are you here to keep an eye on me?

01:08:37.080 --> 01:08:39.830
You think I would skip a sumo match

01:08:39.830 --> 01:08:43.950
to come all the way out here
and waste my time on you?

01:08:44.520 --> 01:08:48.330
I'm here for the vixen's head.

01:08:50.330 --> 01:08:52.090
Hallelujah!

01:08:52.530 --> 01:08:53.810
I'm next!

01:08:53.810 --> 01:08:54.750
And then me!

01:08:54.750 --> 01:08:56.710
Hey! What are you doing?!

01:08:56.710 --> 01:09:00.600
Wouldn't you want to be sent
to heaven by Kyoshiro's rod?!

01:09:00.600 --> 01:09:03.080
Uh, he's using a real blade!

01:09:03.080 --> 01:09:04.530
They're literally going to heaven!

01:09:04.530 --> 01:09:05.530
And what's going on?!

01:09:05.530 --> 01:09:07.800
The others have been understanding

01:09:07.800 --> 01:09:10.130
of our situation and have shown mercy,

01:09:10.330 --> 01:09:12.730
but that guy won't stop
slaughtering trannies!

01:09:12.730 --> 01:09:13.980
Stay back.

01:09:14.140 --> 01:09:15.310
Agomi?!

01:09:15.310 --> 01:09:17.460
I recognize his technique.

01:09:17.980 --> 01:09:22.000
A special assassination technique
for slaying trannies.

01:09:22.000 --> 01:09:23.230
Blade of the Male Escort!

01:09:22.010 --> 01:09:24.470
Blade of the Male Escort!

01:09:23.230 --> 01:09:24.490
That sounds familiar!

01:09:25.070 --> 01:09:26.380
A thousand years ago,

01:09:26.380 --> 01:09:28.480
during the great war between
male escort and tranny,

01:09:28.480 --> 01:09:32.160
this legendary technique was born
during the Battle of Bootyloo.

01:09:32.670 --> 01:09:35.000
I didn't realize that someone
had inherited the technique it.

01:09:35.470 --> 01:09:37.240
This was the last place I expected

01:09:37.240 --> 01:09:39.010
to run into the dreaded
foe of all trannies.

01:09:40.760 --> 01:09:42.430
That stance, it can't be...!

01:09:42.790 --> 01:09:44.420
You were too hasty.

01:09:44.420 --> 01:09:47.790
Yes, I have inherited the

01:09:47.790 --> 01:09:52.400
Kama-sen-ryu which counters
the Blade of the Male Escort!

01:09:52.640 --> 01:09:54.190
I am Agomi, King of Fist!

01:09:54.190 --> 01:09:55.960
Sorry, never heard of you.

01:09:55.960 --> 01:09:57.070
Ago!

01:09:58.150 --> 01:10:01.530
So you were willing to sever
this cursed chin of mine...

01:10:01.530 --> 01:10:03.870
I have no chins in this life!

01:10:03.870 --> 01:10:05.360
Yeah, you do!

01:10:05.360 --> 01:10:07.950
You've got one long-ass chin there!

01:10:07.950 --> 01:10:09.770
Oh, you're right.

01:10:09.770 --> 01:10:10.580
He didn't cut it off?

01:10:10.580 --> 01:10:14.210
Uh, could you pretend to be dead?

01:10:14.510 --> 01:10:18.420
A male escort is only
allowed to penetrate women.

01:10:18.900 --> 01:10:20.040
A toy?

01:10:21.240 --> 01:10:23.710
Kyoshiro!

01:10:22.060 --> 01:10:25.680
You were acting to keep
us from getting hurt!

01:10:25.680 --> 01:10:27.660
I don't care if you use the sword

01:10:27.660 --> 01:10:29.150
up here or the sword down there!

01:10:29.150 --> 01:10:30.100
Penetrate me!

01:10:30.100 --> 01:10:30.890
Penetrat--

01:10:31.710 --> 01:10:33.320
What are you doing?

01:10:33.320 --> 01:10:34.630
We're getting out of here.

01:10:34.630 --> 01:10:36.190
Mama!

01:10:36.190 --> 01:10:37.920
This fight is over.

01:10:37.920 --> 01:10:39.400
We've lost.

01:10:39.690 --> 01:10:40.920
Saigo-san...

01:10:40.920 --> 01:10:42.700
I can't accept that.

01:10:42.700 --> 01:10:46.120
My old man hasn't
conquered the world yet.

01:10:46.120 --> 01:10:48.230
If you want to help
him conquer the world,

01:10:48.230 --> 01:10:51.120
you shouldn't waste his men out here.

01:10:51.120 --> 01:10:53.880
We don't need these useless chumps.

01:10:54.260 --> 01:10:57.250
Go ahead and turn your
back on us if you wish.

01:10:57.670 --> 01:11:01.260
I'll support my old man by
myself if that's what it takes.

01:11:02.860 --> 01:11:04.450
I don't believe it.

01:11:04.450 --> 01:11:08.890
He backstabbed his own relatives
for the sake of business.

01:11:08.890 --> 01:11:12.470
The wife and daughter
you abandoned are here.

01:11:12.470 --> 01:11:16.190
Doesn't matter what
people say about him...

01:11:16.470 --> 01:11:17.720
This is the end.

01:11:17.720 --> 01:11:20.070
We never want anything
to do with you again.

01:11:20.410 --> 01:11:21.630
I see.

01:11:21.630 --> 01:11:25.380
I assumed that it was
over a long time ago.

01:11:25.750 --> 01:11:29.700
Doesn't matter if he
never looks at me...

01:11:30.220 --> 01:11:31.260
I see...

01:11:31.260 --> 01:11:34.080
So he's still making mischief.

01:11:34.080 --> 01:11:37.290
How can you smile?

01:11:37.290 --> 01:11:41.300
He abandoned us and started
doing terrible things

01:11:41.300 --> 01:11:42.800
for the sake of a woman...

01:11:43.630 --> 01:11:45.300
Before he left for the war,

01:11:45.780 --> 01:11:49.060
he placed his hand here and promised...

01:11:50.240 --> 01:11:52.310
...that he would surely return.

01:11:52.690 --> 01:11:57.690
Pirako, he hasn't returned
from the war yet.

01:11:58.370 --> 01:12:00.700
He's still fighting right now.

01:12:01.190 --> 01:12:08.950
Medicine for Ingesting

01:12:01.440 --> 01:12:04.570
But once he's finished, he'll return.

01:12:04.570 --> 01:12:07.710
After all, the one thing
he knew how to do was

01:12:07.710 --> 01:12:08.950
to keep his promises.

01:12:09.610 --> 01:12:12.700
So don't hate him.

01:12:13.100 --> 01:12:14.870
Once I'm gone,

01:12:14.870 --> 01:12:17.580
there won't be anyone on his side.

01:12:18.570 --> 01:12:20.840
We have his promise...

01:12:21.610 --> 01:12:25.130
You will be the only one
who believes in him...

01:12:26.680 --> 01:12:28.510
He promised...

01:12:28.990 --> 01:12:32.680
You'll come back to me, won't you?

01:12:33.240 --> 01:12:37.930
He promised to return...

01:12:41.640 --> 01:12:42.900
Reinforcements from Kada?!

01:12:43.460 --> 01:12:44.810
Take care of this.

01:12:44.810 --> 01:12:46.320
I need to go to my old man.

01:12:48.820 --> 01:12:49.940
Young lady!

01:12:52.980 --> 01:12:57.540
So we were all played
by that damn vixen.

01:12:58.080 --> 01:12:59.620
Mama!

01:13:00.170 --> 01:13:03.080
Sa-Saigo-san...

01:13:03.080 --> 01:13:06.850
Using a kid to set off
a war in this town

01:13:06.850 --> 01:13:10.340
and manipulate the Four Devas
into wearing each other down

01:13:10.340 --> 01:13:13.740
in order to take control of this town.

01:13:13.740 --> 01:13:17.570
That should be the general
gist of your plan.

01:13:18.340 --> 01:13:20.080
But it's too late.

01:13:20.080 --> 01:13:23.880
Those pathetic monkeys are
being crushed as we speak.

01:13:24.410 --> 01:13:26.130
Along with your daughter.

01:13:26.610 --> 01:13:30.750
I doubt that they're
gonna roll over for you.

01:13:30.750 --> 01:13:36.390
Well, this means I get a private
meeting with a beautiful lady.

01:13:37.330 --> 01:13:39.390
We won't be having that.

01:13:39.800 --> 01:13:42.390
Though I've prepared a little party.

01:13:43.150 --> 01:13:44.480
Shinra?

01:13:45.170 --> 01:13:49.860
Along with Yato and
Dakini in your troops,

01:13:49.860 --> 01:13:52.610
it's clear that you're
not just some gambler.

01:13:52.890 --> 01:13:57.390
My long battle with you ends here.

01:13:57.390 --> 01:13:59.550
This town belongs to me now.

01:13:59.550 --> 01:14:00.880
Or should I say...

01:14:00.880 --> 01:14:02.740
It belongs to Kada,

01:14:02.740 --> 01:14:07.130
captain of the 4th squad of
the space pirates Harusame?

01:14:08.240 --> 01:14:11.630
You've finally revealed
your true colors, vixen?

01:14:11.920 --> 01:14:13.630
I know the reason

01:14:13.630 --> 01:14:19.250
you were willing to sink so
low to protect this town.

01:14:19.250 --> 01:14:23.050
You were protecting this
town from us Amanto.

01:14:23.320 --> 01:14:26.390
I learned two things from the war.

01:14:26.390 --> 01:14:31.660
First, at this rate, we'll
be swallowed by you Amanto.

01:14:31.660 --> 01:14:34.720
Second, we are completely powerless.

01:14:35.410 --> 01:14:38.560
Take care of her...
Take care of our town...

01:14:38.560 --> 01:14:40.830
If you still want to protect
what's dear to you,

01:14:40.830 --> 01:14:42.690
you'll have to change.

01:14:43.310 --> 01:14:47.360
I gave up on being a human
so I could defeat you.

01:14:47.690 --> 01:14:50.360
Kada, I can't say much
for any other town,

01:14:50.360 --> 01:14:52.700
but this place won't go
down without a fight.

01:14:54.330 --> 01:14:57.540
Your vaunted Four Devas have
perished, leaving you alone.

01:14:58.200 --> 01:15:00.240
What can you possibly accomplish?

01:15:00.690 --> 01:15:04.540
Have you been paying any
attention to this town?

01:15:05.290 --> 01:15:07.420
Don't underestimate the Kabuki District.

01:15:10.480 --> 01:15:11.470
Who are you people?!

01:15:11.740 --> 01:15:14.520
Sorry to keep you waiting, dark dude.

01:15:14.970 --> 01:15:18.480
I've been waiting for you, silver kid.

01:15:18.770 --> 01:15:21.650
I'd like to return the favor,

01:15:21.650 --> 01:15:25.020
but I guess the situation's changed.

01:15:25.640 --> 01:15:27.650
You've got sharp eyes.

01:15:28.760 --> 01:15:31.550
So while we were engaged
in a pointless fight,

01:15:31.550 --> 01:15:35.450
they took control of this town.

01:15:35.680 --> 01:15:37.430
Sa-Saigo-san...

01:15:37.430 --> 01:15:38.080
Why?

01:15:38.080 --> 01:15:42.230
Hostages are only useful alive.

01:15:42.230 --> 01:15:46.510
I consider you a hostage
to use against Jirocho.

01:15:46.510 --> 01:15:49.200
Besides, I've had enough.

01:15:49.200 --> 01:15:52.000
I don't want to see any old ladies

01:15:52.000 --> 01:15:55.220
or naughty kids bite the dust.

01:15:55.760 --> 01:15:58.920
Our enemy is elsewhere...

01:15:59.380 --> 01:16:01.210
Mama! Hang in there, Mama!

01:16:01.210 --> 01:16:04.100
But it's too late when you realize it.

01:16:07.020 --> 01:16:08.620
Good grief.

01:16:08.810 --> 01:16:11.740
Could you stop whining?

01:16:12.060 --> 01:16:15.430
And you call yourself
Kabuki District residents?

01:16:15.430 --> 01:16:17.380
That voice is...

01:16:19.130 --> 01:16:22.630
Bold and bullheaded,
adamant and adaptable.

01:16:23.180 --> 01:16:25.640
Isn't that our creed?

01:16:26.240 --> 01:16:27.760
O-O...

01:16:28.250 --> 01:16:29.770
Otose!

01:16:30.840 --> 01:16:33.070
Shinpachi, Kagura...

01:16:33.070 --> 01:16:35.030
I'm leaving Saigo's kid to you.

01:16:35.390 --> 01:16:36.150
We're running out of time.

01:16:36.490 --> 01:16:37.680
Gin-chan...

01:16:37.680 --> 01:16:39.150
We promised.

01:16:39.700 --> 01:16:42.220
I'm trusting you to do as I ask,

01:16:42.220 --> 01:16:44.680
so have some faith in me.

01:16:45.540 --> 01:16:46.590
Gin-san...

01:16:48.850 --> 01:16:50.580
We'll meet back up in
the Kabuki district.

01:16:54.920 --> 01:16:57.530
I'm not sure why you're here,

01:16:57.530 --> 01:17:00.840
but you're trying to allow
those kids to escape?

01:17:01.140 --> 01:17:02.590
It's not like that.

01:17:03.290 --> 01:17:04.580
They wouldn't be able to hold

01:17:04.580 --> 01:17:06.090
themselves back against you people.

01:17:06.720 --> 01:17:09.350
It's R-18 time.

01:17:09.980 --> 01:17:12.760
I don't know the details,
but one thing's for sure.

01:17:12.760 --> 01:17:16.230
I'm killing the old man and you, and we're all killing each other.

01:17:18.230 --> 01:17:20.490
You got balls to talk like that to

01:17:20.490 --> 01:17:23.580
the mighty Jirocho and
the Harusame, kid.

01:17:23.580 --> 01:17:26.890
But it's easy to understand.

01:17:26.890 --> 01:17:28.120
Count me in, kid.

01:17:28.540 --> 01:17:30.450
I'm gonna slaughter you all.

01:17:30.660 --> 01:17:32.980
We're all alone here
with no help in sight.

01:17:32.980 --> 01:17:36.460
Just cut down anything that moves.

01:17:36.710 --> 01:17:40.530
The last one standing is the winner.

01:17:40.530 --> 01:17:42.710
Nice and simple, the way I like it.

01:17:42.880 --> 01:17:45.000
You probably had bad grades.

01:17:45.000 --> 01:17:47.040
Not as bad as yours.

01:17:49.300 --> 01:17:50.660
What's so funny?!

01:17:52.100 --> 01:17:53.850
Why are you laughing?!

01:17:53.850 --> 01:17:58.050
Don't you realize the
situation you're in?!

01:17:58.050 --> 01:18:00.320
You and your town are finished!

01:18:04.800 --> 01:18:08.160
Damn old man!

01:18:08.160 --> 01:18:10.330
Kid!

01:18:17.790 --> 01:18:19.320
Don't die...

01:18:19.320 --> 01:18:21.220
...until I kill you.

01:18:21.980 --> 01:18:23.200
Why are you here?!

01:18:23.640 --> 01:18:25.200
Madame Otose...

01:18:25.430 --> 01:18:28.990
Stop this silly fighting.

01:18:28.990 --> 01:18:32.210
Let's make peace and
celebrate at my bar.

01:18:32.210 --> 01:18:33.710
H-Huh?!

01:18:33.910 --> 01:18:35.870
Pirako, you're coming too.

01:18:35.870 --> 01:18:38.320
Since you made a real mess of things

01:18:38.320 --> 01:18:41.830
you'll have to make up for it
with one hell of a show.

01:18:41.840 --> 01:18:43.760
Otose...

01:18:43.760 --> 01:18:45.760
Whatcha babbling about, old lady?

01:18:46.100 --> 01:18:48.460
We don't have time for that!

01:18:49.170 --> 01:18:51.650
Finish up your business then.

01:18:51.650 --> 01:18:53.520
How long are you guys going to lie there?

01:18:53.930 --> 01:18:56.890
This old lady came out here

01:18:56.890 --> 01:18:59.020
despite being seriously injured.

01:18:59.350 --> 01:19:01.670
Enough of your petty bickering.

01:19:01.670 --> 01:19:06.030
There's a serious fight in the
works, with Edo on the line.

01:19:06.550 --> 01:19:10.630
If you don't protect
this town, who will?

01:19:10.630 --> 01:19:12.630
We may be moving in
different directions,

01:19:12.630 --> 01:19:14.540
but we all started in the same place.

01:19:14.770 --> 01:19:18.040
The yakuza, trannies, cabaret girls...

01:19:18.660 --> 01:19:21.800
We all love this town.

01:19:23.370 --> 01:19:26.790
That's all there is to it.

01:19:28.800 --> 01:19:30.560
Otose-san! Look out!

01:19:32.260 --> 01:19:34.620
Hey, if you wanna snuff

01:19:34.620 --> 01:19:37.270
one of the Four Devas while I'm around,

01:19:37.270 --> 01:19:39.520
come back in a hundred years!

01:19:39.830 --> 01:19:41.560
B-Bro!

01:19:41.930 --> 01:19:44.330
What are you fools doing?!

01:19:44.330 --> 01:19:47.310
You always return the
favor, seven for three!

01:19:47.800 --> 01:19:49.060
Well, Gran?

01:19:51.290 --> 01:19:52.730
Show them our...

01:19:52.730 --> 01:19:56.730
No, show them the Kabuki
District's might.

01:19:59.890 --> 01:20:01.730
Wh-Who's there?

01:20:02.010 --> 01:20:05.230
A bandit who's opened
the door to paradise...

01:20:05.480 --> 01:20:06.750
Catherine the lock picker!

01:20:06.750 --> 01:20:08.240
Sorry to keep you waiting.

01:20:10.240 --> 01:20:12.240
Why did you shut the door
without saying anything?!

01:20:12.440 --> 01:20:14.990
Do you realize how hard it
was for me to get here?!

01:20:15.450 --> 01:20:16.980
They found me!

01:20:16.980 --> 01:20:18.340
Hey! Open the door!

01:20:18.340 --> 01:20:19.550
Help!

01:20:19.550 --> 01:20:20.750
Stay away!

01:20:20.750 --> 01:20:21.730
Don't come any closer!

01:20:24.460 --> 01:20:25.960
Wh-Who's there?

01:20:26.380 --> 01:20:29.970
You scared him because of your
funny clothes, Catherine.

01:20:30.510 --> 01:20:31.470
That's right.

01:20:32.100 --> 01:20:33.830
Don't worry!

01:20:33.830 --> 01:20:37.470
The Kabuki Cats are here now!

01:20:41.880 --> 01:20:42.680
B-Bro!

01:20:42.830 --> 01:20:44.820
What are you fools doing?!

01:20:44.820 --> 01:20:48.280
You're gonna stand around while
the Amanto take over our town?!

01:20:48.880 --> 01:20:50.790
Ka-Katsuo...

01:20:51.060 --> 01:20:54.350
Young lady, we were the
castoffs of society

01:20:54.350 --> 01:20:56.810
until the boss took us in.

01:20:57.290 --> 01:21:00.350
We're prepared to throw away

01:21:00.350 --> 01:21:04.800
our worthless lives for the
boss, and for his daughter.

01:21:04.800 --> 01:21:06.200
However...

01:21:06.200 --> 01:21:09.330
We aren't gonna abandon
the town our boss

01:21:09.330 --> 01:21:11.330
has dedicated his life to protecting.

01:21:11.330 --> 01:21:15.310
We have a duty to protect
the Kabuki District!

01:21:16.000 --> 01:21:17.560
Take a good, hard look!

01:21:17.560 --> 01:21:20.820
This is the town your old
man has been protecting!

01:21:20.820 --> 01:21:22.070
Let's do this!

01:21:22.070 --> 01:21:26.740
The whole universe will learn
to fear the Jirocho Gang!

01:21:27.640 --> 01:21:31.330
The Kabuki District belongs to us!

01:21:32.080 --> 01:21:32.900
Heh...

01:21:34.330 --> 01:21:37.930
They're the ones who made
a mess of this town.

01:21:37.930 --> 01:21:40.840
That's why I can't stand yakuza.

01:21:45.100 --> 01:21:48.110
The Kabuki District belongs to you?

01:21:50.160 --> 01:21:51.380
No.

01:21:51.380 --> 01:21:53.770
It belongs to us trannies!

01:21:53.770 --> 01:21:58.320
It's finally time for us to go crazy!

01:21:58.320 --> 01:22:01.280
Show them the true power of a tranny!

01:22:04.100 --> 01:22:07.030
Loud and clear, everyone.

01:22:08.220 --> 01:22:12.200
This is the Kabuki District!

01:23:07.570 --> 01:23:10.030
Fr-Freaks...

01:23:11.050 --> 01:23:15.140
Kill them in the name of the Harusame!

01:23:55.520 --> 01:23:57.150
Finish them!

01:23:59.710 --> 01:24:00.670
Pops,

01:24:01.180 --> 01:24:03.140
we promise to protect everything

01:24:03.140 --> 01:24:05.000
which was dear to you.

01:24:05.460 --> 01:24:06.540
Jirocho...

01:24:07.560 --> 01:24:12.510
Take care of her... Take
care of our town...

01:24:29.200 --> 01:24:30.200
They did it!

01:24:30.990 --> 01:24:33.200
There were only two of them.

01:24:33.540 --> 01:24:38.210
My elite soldiers lost
to these base monkeys.

01:24:38.440 --> 01:24:41.450
This can't be... This can't be...

01:24:45.730 --> 01:24:46.660
That's...

01:24:47.200 --> 01:24:48.350
Otose!

01:24:53.790 --> 01:24:59.170
I never expected this filthy
town to be home to such heroes.

01:24:59.630 --> 01:25:01.680
Mark my words, Jirocho...

01:25:02.330 --> 01:25:06.180
The Harusame will return this favor!

01:25:08.080 --> 01:25:09.810
W-Wait...

01:25:18.730 --> 01:25:22.890
All this effort to chase
a vixen out of town.

01:25:22.890 --> 01:25:24.820
I don't want to get any older.

01:25:25.620 --> 01:25:30.100
But you young'ns are disappointing.

01:25:32.270 --> 01:25:34.650
When I was a young lad...

01:25:34.650 --> 01:25:36.470
The elderly always let nostalgia

01:25:36.470 --> 01:25:38.460
cloud their memory.

01:25:38.720 --> 01:25:41.060
I don't want to get any older.

01:25:41.430 --> 01:25:43.630
Hey, kid.

01:25:43.630 --> 01:25:45.970
Is that his jutte?

01:25:46.980 --> 01:25:49.150
Why do you have it?

01:25:50.580 --> 01:25:54.230
I made a one-sided promise,
and then I swiped it.

01:25:54.460 --> 01:25:55.230
Heh.

01:25:57.960 --> 01:25:59.290
Same here.

01:26:02.490 --> 01:26:06.240
Whenever I smoke, the
memories come back.

01:26:06.850 --> 01:26:09.370
I would watch from behind

01:26:09.390 --> 01:26:12.170
as he walked around, toying with his jutte

01:26:12.170 --> 01:26:14.210
while smoking with his left.

01:26:15.090 --> 01:26:17.110
It was rather striking to see him

01:26:17.110 --> 01:26:19.170
with the Kabuki District as a backdrop.

01:26:19.610 --> 01:26:22.270
He loved this town,

01:26:22.270 --> 01:26:25.760
and I'm sure that this town loved him.

01:26:25.760 --> 01:26:30.500
We can smoke and fiddle with a jutte,

01:26:30.500 --> 01:26:33.270
but we can never be like him?

01:26:33.500 --> 01:26:36.930
He died the way he lived.

01:26:36.930 --> 01:26:38.820
Like a man,

01:26:38.820 --> 01:26:41.640
who sacrificed his life
for someone like me

01:26:41.640 --> 01:26:43.240
while leaving loved ones behind.

01:26:44.090 --> 01:26:46.280
I killed him.

01:26:48.060 --> 01:26:52.660
So I had to give up on being
a man, on being human,

01:26:52.660 --> 01:26:56.250
in order to protect what he left behind.

01:26:57.000 --> 01:26:59.990
Even if the town hated me for it...

01:27:00.190 --> 01:27:01.300
Damn...

01:27:01.670 --> 01:27:04.150
So you weren't trying to kill Gran.

01:27:05.210 --> 01:27:09.300
She's always been a pain in the ass.

01:27:09.600 --> 01:27:13.310
Squawking in my ear whenever
I did something...

01:27:14.050 --> 01:27:17.980
My resolve would waver when I saw her.

01:27:18.500 --> 01:27:19.990
When I watched you guys,

01:27:19.990 --> 01:27:24.610
I would get the urge to go
back to being the old Jirocho.

01:27:26.310 --> 01:27:28.650
You're getting in my way, Tatsugoro.

01:27:30.640 --> 01:27:33.330
Let's settle this once and for all.

01:27:34.040 --> 01:27:38.830
We'll see who's worthy of
inheriting his pipe and jutte.

01:27:39.330 --> 01:27:41.710
I'm not interested in any inheritances.

01:27:42.030 --> 01:27:44.840
I just wanted to keep
my promise this time.

01:27:45.980 --> 01:27:50.840
It's obvious that neither of
us is going to cave or give in.

01:27:51.230 --> 01:27:52.730
In that case...

01:27:52.730 --> 01:27:55.740
...there's only one way
for us to move forward.

01:28:00.330 --> 01:28:03.020
I will keep my promise and survive.

01:28:03.390 --> 01:28:04.380
In return...

01:28:04.380 --> 01:28:07.090
...you will keep your promise...

01:28:07.760 --> 01:28:09.340
...and die.

01:28:09.790 --> 01:28:13.160
Both of you are chained to
this town by the same thing.

01:28:13.640 --> 01:28:17.560
A promise made to a certain man.

01:28:18.450 --> 01:28:21.350
An iron vow of your own choosing.

01:28:22.390 --> 01:28:24.120
The chains of a warrior.

01:28:26.570 --> 01:28:28.570
Old man!

01:28:43.330 --> 01:28:45.870
Your promise was broken.

01:28:46.240 --> 01:28:47.590
I win.

01:28:53.340 --> 01:28:54.600
Bastard...

01:28:55.430 --> 01:28:57.350
Why didn't you cut me down?

01:28:57.900 --> 01:28:59.350
Like I said...

01:29:00.060 --> 01:29:03.350
I'm going to keep my promise this time.

01:29:03.350 --> 01:29:04.690
Pops,

01:29:04.690 --> 01:29:06.420
we promise to protect

01:29:06.420 --> 01:29:08.480
everything which was dear to you.

01:29:10.970 --> 01:29:13.330
Quit smoking, old timer.

01:29:25.360 --> 01:29:29.530
I'd appreciate it if you
never woke up again.

01:29:29.530 --> 01:29:31.950
Usually, you wouldn't put
a guy in the same room

01:29:31.950 --> 01:29:33.290
as the person he stabbed.

01:29:34.660 --> 01:29:37.000
This can't be a hospital.

01:29:37.320 --> 01:29:38.940
Must be some kind of haunted house.

01:29:39.480 --> 01:29:40.550
What was that, Seirogan?!

01:29:41.140 --> 01:29:46.050
Looks like everyone managed
to survive somehow.

01:29:46.400 --> 01:29:48.160
Had nothing to do with us.

01:29:48.470 --> 01:29:50.050
Our lives were saved.

01:29:50.800 --> 01:29:52.000
Your daughter spent

01:29:52.000 --> 01:29:55.100
three days taking care
of you without any sleep.

01:29:55.560 --> 01:29:58.810
And your daughter kept an eye on me

01:29:58.810 --> 01:30:02.320
to make sure I didn't run off
again and exacerbate my injuries.

01:30:02.660 --> 01:30:05.000
A futile effort.

01:30:05.000 --> 01:30:07.370
We can stab you, tie you up,

01:30:07.370 --> 01:30:08.640
and you'll still get back up.

01:30:08.640 --> 01:30:11.330
You're one to talk, stubborn mule.

01:30:11.550 --> 01:30:14.770
I know that I'm stubborn,

01:30:14.770 --> 01:30:20.190
but you make me look like
a reasonable fellow.

01:30:20.190 --> 01:30:25.340
Everybody turned out to
be as twisted as he was.

01:30:25.990 --> 01:30:29.830
Actually, you're worse
than Tatsugoro was,

01:30:29.830 --> 01:30:33.000
since you beat me in a battle of wills.

01:30:33.000 --> 01:30:36.310
You look pretty happy for
someone who was beaten.

01:30:37.140 --> 01:30:38.350
Yeah...

01:30:38.920 --> 01:30:41.740
It's been so long since
I've had a real fight.

01:30:42.360 --> 01:30:46.360
A real fight between men and warriors.

01:30:46.850 --> 01:30:50.370
I can only laugh after losing
in such a satisfying way.

01:30:50.370 --> 01:30:54.570
I've given up so much to be
able to keep my promise...

01:30:54.570 --> 01:30:59.920
But he managed to save everything
to keep his promise,

01:30:59.920 --> 01:31:00.960
including me.

01:31:01.990 --> 01:31:05.090
No, I was just running away...

01:31:05.090 --> 01:31:07.970
I was scared of losing
anyone else dear again...

01:31:08.540 --> 01:31:13.970
He shattered the ungainly
chains around my neck.

01:31:13.970 --> 01:31:18.980
They made it clear that they could
protect this town without me.

01:31:20.440 --> 01:31:22.180
Twenty years...

01:31:22.180 --> 01:31:24.700
I spend twenty years keeping my promise,

01:31:24.700 --> 01:31:26.630
and this is how it ends.

01:31:26.940 --> 01:31:28.570
In the end,

01:31:28.570 --> 01:31:31.180
I just made everyone around me unhappy,

01:31:31.180 --> 01:31:33.990
while failing to keep my promise.

01:31:35.130 --> 01:31:36.500
Otose...

01:31:36.950 --> 01:31:40.500
You've done a lot for me.

01:31:40.790 --> 01:31:44.510
But I kept running in circles.

01:31:44.510 --> 01:31:48.510
I was never able to return the favor.

01:31:49.570 --> 01:31:54.010
Sorry I couldn't make you happy.

01:31:55.040 --> 01:31:57.540
Jirocho, I'm...

01:32:01.020 --> 01:32:03.020
Damn! What are people doing?!

01:32:03.020 --> 01:32:05.480
It was about to get good!

01:32:05.850 --> 01:32:07.860
I told you to stop pushing!

01:32:07.860 --> 01:32:10.620
It's your fault for bringing
such a big camera!

01:32:10.620 --> 01:32:11.350
Shut up!

01:32:11.350 --> 01:32:13.640
How often are we gonna get to see
the boss in a romantic scene?!

01:32:13.640 --> 01:32:14.750
Men are so hopeless.

01:32:14.750 --> 01:32:16.810
The sensitivity of a brick.

01:32:16.810 --> 01:32:18.200
What's that in your hand?!

01:32:18.620 --> 01:32:20.390
Please stop this, everyone.

01:32:20.390 --> 01:32:21.290
Recording mode off.

01:32:21.290 --> 01:32:22.650
I just heard something!

01:32:22.650 --> 01:32:23.820
You were recording!

01:32:23.820 --> 01:32:24.880
You were recording the entire time!

01:32:24.880 --> 01:32:27.260
What are you people doing here so late?!

01:32:27.260 --> 01:32:28.940
Wait, that's alcohol!

01:32:28.940 --> 01:32:30.180
Don't you realize what
kind of place this is?!

01:32:30.180 --> 01:32:32.490
This is ours!

01:32:32.490 --> 01:32:34.840
Do you realize how much
effort it took to get

01:32:34.840 --> 01:32:36.890
the old lady on top of the roof?!

01:32:37.420 --> 01:32:38.770
Jirocho...

01:32:38.770 --> 01:32:42.390
You and Gintoki will never change.

01:32:42.610 --> 01:32:46.020
You're both selfish jerks.

01:32:46.020 --> 01:32:49.890
The difference is that he had
people to help him realize

01:32:49.890 --> 01:32:55.950
that other people needed
him the way he needed them.

01:32:56.390 --> 01:33:00.310
Now, you can see that
there's no need to worry.

01:33:00.940 --> 01:33:02.350
You did a fine job of
protecting this town

01:33:02.350 --> 01:33:05.210
until the next generation
could take over.

01:33:05.880 --> 01:33:07.260
You kept your promise.

01:33:08.580 --> 01:33:11.380
So you can let go now.

01:33:11.840 --> 01:33:17.970
You have other promises to keep.

01:33:19.030 --> 01:33:23.220
I'm very happy right now, Jirocho.

01:33:23.930 --> 01:33:26.940
I met Tatsugoro here
in the Kabuki District.

01:33:27.350 --> 01:33:29.440
And I met them.

01:33:29.940 --> 01:33:34.490
And I met our beloved Jirocho again.

01:33:39.400 --> 01:33:43.520
Thanks for everything, Jirocho.

01:33:47.670 --> 01:33:49.210
This isn't good.

01:33:49.210 --> 01:33:51.820
My eyesight's starting to fail me.

01:33:52.420 --> 01:33:55.550
First, I can't control my bowels,

01:33:55.550 --> 01:33:57.970
now I'm leaking up here.

01:33:57.970 --> 01:34:01.970
Greater Edo Hospital

01:33:59.370 --> 01:34:01.970
I don't want to get any older.

01:34:03.540 --> 01:34:05.640
We cannot allow them
to get away with this.

01:34:06.020 --> 01:34:07.890
Just you wait, Devas.

01:34:08.180 --> 01:34:10.570
I can no longer turn back.

01:34:10.570 --> 01:34:12.610
I will do anything to obtain
the Kabuki District.

01:34:13.420 --> 01:34:15.610
I've been waiting for you, Lady Kada.

01:34:16.680 --> 01:34:17.610
You're...!

01:34:17.850 --> 01:34:21.120
Sorry, but could you not interfere?

01:34:21.130 --> 01:34:25.120
I finally get to see my old man look...

01:34:25.120 --> 01:34:26.610
Silence!

01:34:26.610 --> 01:34:29.620
Don't you understand that you're
the one who's interfering?!

01:34:30.040 --> 01:34:31.630
I do.

01:34:31.850 --> 01:34:33.630
My interference is over.

01:34:34.070 --> 01:34:37.170
But I'm taking you with me!

01:34:37.380 --> 01:34:40.180
You're the only one who's leaving!

01:34:42.600 --> 01:34:44.680
Br-Bro!

01:34:44.680 --> 01:34:46.270
Sacrificing yourself
to take out the enemy...

01:34:46.680 --> 01:34:48.320
won't be enough to make up

01:34:48.320 --> 01:34:50.190
for everything you've done, bitch!

01:34:50.620 --> 01:34:52.150
There you have it.

01:34:52.620 --> 01:34:54.690
Whatcha gonna do now, Pirako-chan?

01:34:55.870 --> 01:34:58.470
My job is finished.

01:34:58.470 --> 01:35:01.200
You can have your way with me.

01:35:01.420 --> 01:35:03.090
Sad.

01:35:03.090 --> 01:35:06.200
Don't you need to settle
things with your old man?

01:35:06.660 --> 01:35:08.460
I have.

01:35:08.460 --> 01:35:11.710
You took all the glory though.

01:35:12.300 --> 01:35:14.770
You're the one who saved my old man.

01:35:14.770 --> 01:35:17.210
I didn't expect you to protect him...

01:35:17.510 --> 01:35:19.670
No, it wasn't just you.

01:35:20.240 --> 01:35:21.880
This town has

01:35:21.880 --> 01:35:25.160
wonderful people who help one another

01:35:25.160 --> 01:35:26.770
despite their differences.

01:35:26.770 --> 01:35:28.720
They do more than take away...

01:35:28.720 --> 01:35:31.340
If I could be like them...

01:35:33.500 --> 01:35:35.590
But it's okay now.

01:35:35.590 --> 01:35:37.630
The father I wanted to see...

01:35:37.630 --> 01:35:40.490
The father who Mom and I were waiting for...

01:35:41.030 --> 01:35:44.120
...is back.

01:35:45.870 --> 01:35:48.190
Bro... Everyone...

01:35:48.190 --> 01:35:50.800
I can't apologize for what I've done,

01:35:50.800 --> 01:35:53.010
but let me say this.

01:35:53.910 --> 01:35:56.410
Thank you for letting me see my

01:35:56.410 --> 01:35:58.250
father one last time!

01:35:58.720 --> 01:36:02.960
I couldn't be my father's
daughter or the Bro's underling,

01:36:02.960 --> 01:36:07.210
but I was very happy to be
a resident of this town,

01:36:07.210 --> 01:36:08.690
if only for a moment.

01:36:09.200 --> 01:36:11.300
Please let me take responsibility
for what I've done...

01:36:12.040 --> 01:36:14.060
Sorry, but I'm not
sadistic enough to beat

01:36:14.060 --> 01:36:15.910
up a crying little girl.

01:36:15.910 --> 01:36:17.320
Besides, I'm tired.

01:36:17.830 --> 01:36:19.740
Go wait at the place listed there.

01:36:20.220 --> 01:36:23.070
I'll deal with you once I'm healed up.

01:36:23.340 --> 01:36:25.450
You better be done crying by then.

01:36:29.580 --> 01:36:31.790
Let's try that place next time.

01:36:31.790 --> 01:36:32.580
Sure.

01:36:32.580 --> 01:36:36.580
Bar Chono

01:36:32.970 --> 01:36:34.030
What?

01:36:34.030 --> 01:36:36.580
You want to know who the strongest
man in the Kabuki District is?

01:36:36.910 --> 01:36:39.260
You must be new in town.

01:36:39.260 --> 01:36:42.340
Won't last long with that attitude.

01:36:42.860 --> 01:36:44.220
Forget it.

01:36:44.220 --> 01:36:45.840
This town is on a whole different level.

01:36:45.840 --> 01:36:46.840
It's too dangerous.

01:36:47.370 --> 01:36:49.700
With the fall of the Deva Kada

01:36:49.700 --> 01:36:51.460
and the retirement of the Deva Jirocho,

01:36:51.460 --> 01:36:55.840
the fragile balance of power
is beginning to crumble.

01:36:56.310 --> 01:36:59.600
The town's never been this tense before.

01:37:45.570 --> 01:37:47.860
Is that you, Bro?

01:37:48.820 --> 01:37:50.110
'Tis an honor.

01:37:50.500 --> 01:37:53.840
I was born and raised in
the Kabuki District of Edo,

01:37:53.840 --> 01:37:57.230
where I lived as a ruffian
in a town of ruffians,

01:37:57.230 --> 01:38:01.370
always surrounded by steel.

01:38:01.370 --> 01:38:05.900
I am ashamed to admit
that I have walked astray

01:38:05.900 --> 01:38:08.460
and was guided by my brothers

01:38:08.460 --> 01:38:10.160
to embark on a journey of redemption

01:38:10.160 --> 01:38:12.430
to regain that which I have lost.

01:38:13.720 --> 01:38:18.920
I have been called boss,
warrior, and many other names,

01:38:18.920 --> 01:38:20.930
but I have given them up.

01:38:22.790 --> 01:38:25.140
I am the father of Pirako Chin,

01:38:25.140 --> 01:38:28.760
Jirocho.

01:38:30.730 --> 01:38:33.360
It's rude, but may I ask who you are?

01:38:33.980 --> 01:38:39.170
I-I am the newest member
of the Odd Jobs family

01:38:39.170 --> 01:38:41.570
in the Kabuki District of Edo...

01:38:41.570 --> 01:38:44.910
On a journey to find my missing father...

01:38:46.610 --> 01:38:52.860
I was guided here by the
kindness of my brothers.

01:38:54.230 --> 01:38:56.380
I am the daughter of Jirocho,

01:38:56.380 --> 01:38:59.110
Pirako Chin!

01:39:03.120 --> 01:39:06.560
We must have been brought
together by fate.

01:39:06.560 --> 01:39:08.190
Would you mind

01:39:09.430 --> 01:39:12.690
if I accompanied you on your journey?

01:39:44.610 --> 01:39:46.230
I'm home.
